  - TypeFullName: BasisCrashReportStore
    MemberName: BasisCrashReportStore
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Captures local error/exception reports to disk during a session and,
      if the previous\n session ended without a clean shutdown (i.e. it crashed),
      re-sends what it had captured\n once the client reconnects and the server has
      reporting enabled. This is what lets a\n hard crash \u2014 which can never
      report live, because the app is gone \u2014 still reach the\n server's per-player
      crash store on the next launch.\n\n Layout under `Application.persistentDataPath/CrashReports`:\n  
      session.active : present while a session is running; deleted on a clean quit.\n  
      pending.jsonl  : reports captured during the CURRENT session.\n   replay.jsonl  
      : an outbox of reports carried over from a crashed session, awaiting\n                   
      send. It is deleted only once the reports have actually been handed off\n                   
      for sending, so a crash before that point simply retries next launch,\n                   
      while a successful send removes the outbox so the same reports are\n                   
      never sent again on a later reboot.\n\n Records are stored one per line as
      `severity \\t base64(system) \\t base64(message) \\t\n base64(stack)` \u2014
      base64 keeps newlines/arbitrary characters from breaking the line\n format
      without pulling in a JSON dependency."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
