    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Do trackers actually pose the LEGS?\n\n HasFBIKTrackers is a WHOLE-BODY
      flag -- it is true for a chest, shoulder, elbow or hips tracker just as\n readily
      as for a foot. Asking it a LEG question gives the wrong answer, and the failure
      is silent and\n severe: the animator suppresses the walk cycle \"because we're
      in FBT\", while leg IK simultaneously\n disables itself during locomotion (so
      the animation can take over) -- and the legs end up with NO driver\n at all.
      They freeze mid-stride.\n\n That went unnoticed for as long as the only things
      producing chest/shoulder/elbow trackers were real FBT\n rigs, which carry leg
      trackers too -- so the suppression happened to be right, for the wrong reason.\n
      MediaPipe spawns chest/shoulder/elbow trackers with no leg trackers anywhere,
      which is what exposed it.\n\n A leg question gets a leg answer. Read live so
      it self-heals on tracker dropout/reconnect."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: IsRoleTracked
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisLocalBoneDriver.HipsControl
    ParamDocs: []
