    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Is the PELVIS specifically tracker-driven?\n\n Distinct from HasLegFBIKTrackers
      on purpose: a hip tracker moves the leg ROOT but does not pose the legs,\n
      so it should not silence the walk cycle. It DOES make the pelvis authoritative,
      so anything that\n synthesises pelvis motion (the landing hip-dip, gait bob/sway/pelvis-rotation)
      must stand down or it\n fights the user's real body."
    Remarks: 
