  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.
    MemberName: ReprojectTrackerOffsetsForCurrentAvatar
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - null
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Re-derives every calibrated FBT tracker's POSITION inverse offset for
      the CURRENT avatar and\n DeviceScale from the scale-free calibration snapshots
      \u2014 the position analog of\n ApplyCalibrationToCurrentAvatar (which re-derives
      the per-effector ROTATION\n offsets). BasisHeightDriver calls this whenever
      the height/scale pipeline re-resolves\n (avatar swap, scale slider, OSC override),
      so FBT keeps fitting without redoing the T-pose.\n The player's live pose is
      irrelevant: only the stored calibration geometry and the current\n avatar's
      T-pose bind (TposeLocalScaled) are used. Each tracker rebuilds against the
      head\n anchor it was captured with (BasisInput.CalibratedUnscaledHead*), so
      a mid-session recapture\n keeps its own frame instead of inheriting the ritual
      one. The offset ROTATION is untouched \u2014\n it maps tracker rotation to
      the bone-sim body frame, which is avatar- and scale-independent.\n No-op for
      trackers without a snapshot."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
