  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisAvatarSetupBudget
    MemberName: BasisAvatarSetupBudget
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Main-thread admission budget for the post-load avatar setup tail \u2014
      the trim +\n calibration + bone-system registration that runs once a bundle
      has finished loading."
    Remarks: "The concurrency gates in BasisAvatarFactory only throttle the async
      bundle\n I/O and are released before `InitializePlayerAvatar` runs, so a bulk
      in-range\n transition (the View Range slider 0->100 at 1k players) would dump
      hundreds of\n calibrations onto a single frame even though the downloads themselves
      were paced. This caps\n how many setups start per frame; over-budget loads
      yield to the next frame and resume.\n Pure main-thread frame pacing (no locks):
      every awaiter resumes on Unity's synchronization\n context, so the counter
      is only ever touched by one thread."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
