  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisTrackerPairing
    MemberName: BasisTrackerPairing
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Stores symmetric tracker\u2192tracker links keyed by UniqueDeviceIdentifier
      so\n pairings survive disconnect/reconnect. When two trackers are paired the\n
      constellation classifier in BasisAvatarIKStageCalibration treats them as\n
      a single virtual tracker positioned at the midpoint of the pair, and\n binds
      the resulting role to the canonical (lower-id) device only \u2014 the\n partner
      is left unassigned.\n\n Pairings are persisted to Application.persistentDataPath
      as\n JSON so they survive process restart. The pairing service rehydrates the\n
      in-memory dictionary on first access (lazy load) and writes it back after\n
      every successful Link/Unlink. Trackers that are paired but offline stay\n in
      the file as dormant entries; when they reconnect, the pairing service's\n reconcile
      pass finds the pre-existing pairing and re-creates the merged\n virtual on
      the spot \u2014 no user re-pairing required."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
