  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisHighPlayerCapPerformanceMode
    MemberName: BasisHighPlayerCapPerformanceMode
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Watches the instance population and, once per app run for each population
      tier, offers to\n switch on a \"High Player Cap Performance Mode\" preset that
      trades avatar fidelity for frame\n rate in large instances. Pumped from the
      central tick; no MonoBehaviour.\n\n Each tier asks at most once per app lifetime
      \u2014 the static \"asked\" flags reset on restart,\n so the offer comes back
      the next time the app is launched into a crowded instance. Crossing\n a higher
      tier supersedes the lower ones (their flags are marked asked at the same time),
      so\n joining an already-huge instance shows a single prompt instead of stacking
      several.\n\n Only the pose-update LOD bias tightens between tiers; every other
      value in the preset is the\n same at every tier. The dialogue lists the exact
      values it will apply, sourced from the same\n constants used to apply them,
      so the text can never drift from the effect."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
    MemberName: TryOfferBeforeConnect
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - prospectiveOccupants
    - null
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Offer the performance preset before a connection to a server whose
      probe reported a\n crowd. `prospectiveOccupants` is the reported online count
      plus the\n joining local player, matching the occupant semantics of the post-join
      watcher.\n Returns true when a prompt was shown and the connection is deferred
      \u2014 every choice in\n the prompt (including closing it unanswered) then
      runs `continueConnect`,\n so the click on Connect is never silently swallowed.
      Returns false when nothing needs\n asking and the caller should just connect."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
