  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.BasisInputPumpMode
    MemberName: BasisInputPumpMode
    Kind: Enum
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Drives InputSystem.Update from the event driver. Desktop and OpenXR
      modes pump every frame:\n desktop lives on keyboard/mouse and OpenXR streams
      HMD/controller state through the Input\n System. OpenVR mode reads all VR input
      via the OpenVR API instead, leaving keyboard/mouse as\n the only Input System
      consumers, and those only matter while the user is actually typing or\n clicking
      \u2014 so the pump runs full rate while events are flowing and decays to a
      slow heartbeat\n after a quiet spell. Queued events are never lost; a throttled
      pump only delays them by at\n most IdlePumpInterval."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
