  - TypeFullName: Basis.Editor.Constraints.BasisConstraintInspectorBase
    MemberName: BasisConstraintInspectorBase
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: UnityEditor.Editor
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 1
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Shared chrome for every Basis constraint inspector, in the same card-and-accent
      style as the\n sync components so the SDK reads as one thing.\n\n The layout
      deliberately follows Unity's own constraint inspectors, because that is what
      people\n porting a rig already know: Activate and Zero at the top, then weight,
      then the source list,\n then the per-axis toggles. Activate does what Unity's
      does \u2014 freeze the current pose as the\n neutral one and switch the constraint
      on \u2014 which matters more here than it does in Unity,\n since several Basis
      kinds capture a bind rather than only a rest pose."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
