  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: SampleTrilinear
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - table
    - normalizedPos
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: Trilinear interpolation lookup. Position should be in normalized space
      [-1, 1].
    Remarks: "This is inside a Burst job, so an out-of-range index is not an exception
      you catch \u2014 it aborts the\n process. It therefore must not trust its caller.
      Mathf.Clamp did: it reads\n `if (v < min) v = min; else if (v > max) v = max;`,
      and a NaN fails BOTH comparisons, so it\n passed straight through to `(int)NaN`
      == int.MinValue and indexed the table at -2147483648.\n Anything non-finite
      now lands on the grid origin instead: a slightly wrong elbow for one frame
      beats\n killing the editor."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
