    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Humeral elevation in the TORSO frame: 0 = arm at the side, 90 = horizontal,
      180 =\n straight overhead. Measured against TorsoUp (chest->neck) and NOT PlayerUp
      -- the root's up stays\n vertical while the chest does not, so a PlayerUp elevation
      is meaningless the moment the user\n bends at the waist, which is the exact
      wrong-frame class that made a guard fire on ordinary\n bent-over poses with
      its measurement's sign flipped. TorsoUpValid records which\n frame was actually
      available."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
