    Summary: "Plane of elevation, clinical convention, mirrored per arm so both report
      the same number\n for the same gesture: 0 = pure abduction (arm out to the
      side), +90 = forward flexion, -90 =\n extension behind the body. This is the
      second axis of the segmentation -- a glenohumeral arc is\n position-dependent
      in BOTH elevation and plane, and pooling over either hid a band-specific\n
      breach twice this week."
