  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisArmDiagnostics
    MemberName: TwistGuardAvailable
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE AVAILABILITY BITS ARE THE POINT, NOT DECORATION.\n\n A stage
      that is DECLINED and a stage that is INSIDE ITS ENVELOPE both report a flat
      zero\n correction, and telling them apart after the fact is impossible from
      the correction alone. That\n conflation is a named defect class in this codebase:
      a guard whose soft margin exceeded the\n circle it was guarding fired 0 times
      in 22032 poses, exactly where it was needed, and read as\n \"quiet\". These
      recompute each stage's OWN entry test from the input, so a session in which
      a\n guard was structurally dead shows up as a column of zeros HERE rather than
      as silence there."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
