  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisArmDiagnosticsCore
    MemberName: BasisArmDiagnosticsCore
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Stream-free, allocation-free, Burst-safe capture of one arm's frame.
      Pure in the strongest available\n sense: it takes both of its inputs by `in`
      and writes only to `out`, so it CANNOT perturb the solve.\n See BasisArmDiagnosticsTests.Capture_IsReadOnly_SolveIsBitIdentical,
      which does not take that on\n trust -- it solves the same grid with and without
      capture and compares every result field bitwise,\n and proves its own comparator
      can see a one-ULP difference before it believes a pass.\n\n Written the long
      way -- no Vector3.Angle, no Quaternion.AngleAxis, no Vector3.SignedAngle --
      for the\n same reason BasisArmSolveCore is: this runs inside a Burst job, and
      it must read the geometry with\n the same closed forms the core does or the
      diagnostic and the thing it measures disagree at the\n singularities, which
      are the only places anybody is looking."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
