  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisArmDiagnosticsCore
    MemberName: ElevationBand
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 180f)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F NEVER POOLED. Pooling hid a band-specific breach twice
      this week: a 90 deg humeral bound\n looked defensible on pooled corpus data
      and breached the house 3% firing precedent in TWO\n elevation bands once split
      (4.2% at 60-90, 4.8% at 90-120). Segmenting is not a refinement of\n this analysis,
      it IS the analysis.\n\n Returns -1 for a non-finite or out-of-range input --
      NOT band 0. A NaN frame is not evidence\n about the 0-30 deg band and silently
      filing it there is how a percentile gets poisoned. Written\n reject-unless-good
      so NaN takes the -1 branch rather than being waved through by a comparison
      it\n cannot fail."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
