  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: TwistDeg
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - q
    - k_SqrEpsilon)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: " <summary>\n \u26A0\uFE0F NOT `2 * acos(|dot|)`, AND THE DIFFERENCE
      IS THE VALIDITY OF EVERY NUMBER IN THIS FILE.\n\n acos loses half the float
      mantissa near dot = 1: an error of eps in the dot becomes sqrt(2*eps)\n in
      the angle, so at float32 precision two BIT-IDENTICAL rotations measure up to
      ~0.09 deg apart.\n The composition above chains five quaternion products and
      Unity does not renormalise on multiply,\n so the drift is real and always present.
      atan2 of the vector part against the scalar part is\n well-conditioned at zero
      and costs nothing.\n\n NaN-safe by shape: `!(x > eps)` takes the reject branch
      on NaN, where `x < eps` would wave it\n through -- NaN fails every ordered
      comparison, so a guard must read \"reject unless good\".\n </summary>"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
