    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The TORSO's up (chest->neck, i.e. BasisSwivelHintCore.BuildFrame(...).Up),
      which is the\n frame BasisElbowAnatomyCore's law was measured in and the ONLY
      frame it is true in. PlayerUp is the\n player ROOT's up: it stays vertical
      while the chest does not, so feeding the guard that one makes\n \"above the
      shoulder\" meaningless the moment the user bends at the waist -- and the guard
      then fires\n on ordinary bent-over poses (measured: 0.3475% of the posture
      tier, with the measurement's SIGN\n FLIPPED). Zero -- the struct default --
      falls back to PlayerUp, which is the pre-fix behaviour, so a\n caller that
      cannot build a body frame still gets a guarded arm rather than none."
    Remarks: 
