    MemberName: BindLowerArmRotation
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bind/T-pose world rotation of the LOWER ARM bone. With BindHumerusRotation
      it fixes the\n forearm's ZERO-PRONATION relationship to the humerus, which
      is the only thing that makes the\n no-tracker forearm roll a DEFINED quantity
      instead of one inherited from the animation clip.\n\n It is a RELATIVE rotation
      that gets used (Inverse(BindHumerusRotation) * BindLowerArmRotation), so\n
      it carries no world-frame assumption and no conditioning hazard: a straight-armed
      T-pose, which\n breaks any construction that needs a hinge AXIS (upper arm
      and forearm are collinear there, so\n their cross product is undefined), is
      a complete non-event for a relative quaternion.\n\n Zero -- the struct default
      -- declines, so every existing caller, test and offline sweep is\n bit-identical
      until a rig actually bakes it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
