  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisArmSolveResult
    MemberName: ForearmRollDemandDeg
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "TRACKER path only (0 on every other path): the roll this stage was
      ASKED for, before the\n +/-180 principal-branch wrap, before the soft/hard
      saturation and before the seam cap.\n\n It is published for the same reason
      HumeralTwistDeg is: the envelope the APPLIED roll\n has to satisfy is a function
      of the demand, not a constant. The seam cap deliberately relaxes the\n hard
      bound approaching +/-180 -- that is the price of continuity there, stated in
      the core -- so a\n gate on ForearmRollDeg has to read\n\n     max(TrackerForearmRollMaxDeg,
      2*|Mathf.DeltaAngle(0, ForearmRollDemandDeg)| - 180)\n\n exactly as the humeral
      guard's gate reads max(HumeralTwistHardDeg, 2*|HumeralTwistDeg| - 180). A\n
      FLAT bound on the applied roll is only correct for a stage that has no seam
      cap, and this one now\n has. Reported BEFORE the wrap so a test can also see
      when the hand blend has carried the demand off\n its principal branch, which
      is a separate hole the wrap closes."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
