    Summary: "The hand's axial roll relative to the SOLVED forearm -- as the stream
      will actually\n render it, not as the solver hoped -- measured BEFORE the wrist
      bound. This is the quantity the\n radiocarpal joint has no range for, and it
      is published because the bound's envelope is a\n function of the demand (the
      seam cap relaxes nothing here, but a gate still has to be able to\n see what
      was asked for in order to tell a bound that engaged from one that never had
      to)."
