  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisArmSwivelModel
    MemberName: SwivelRad
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - tipLocal
    - confidence
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "As above, and it also hands back HOW MUCH IT KNOWS. sin and cos are
      fitted as two independent\n polynomials, so nothing forces sqrt(s*s + c*c)
      to stay near 1. Least squares shrinks BOTH toward\n zero exactly where the
      true swivel is genuinely UNPREDICTABLE -- and atan2 near the origin does not\n
      fail, it SPINS. Across the corpus this magnitude falls under 0.2 on 0.004 %
      of frames, so the guard\n essentially never fires; it is here because the failure
      it prevents is a spinning elbow."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
