  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisArmSwivelNeuralModel
    MemberName: BasisArmSwivelNeuralModel
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "AUTO-GENERATED by tools/neural_ik/solver_residual.py -- DO NOT HAND-EDIT.
      Re-fit and re-generate.\n\n A bounded RESIDUAL on BasisArmSwivelModel: swivel
      = poly(t) + 25deg * tanh(MLP(t)). The\n polynomial does the work; the MLP nudges
      it by at most 25 degrees. Because the base is the\n smooth poly and the correction
      is bounded, this is smooth ON THE TRAJECTORY (adds no pops) -- the one\n regime
      where the offline solver metric is faithful, so the measured gain TRANSFERS
      to the live solver\n (unlike a free MLP, which finds sharp poles that game
      the per-frame metric and then flip in Unity).\n\n This is the ONLY neural pole
      that beat the tuned polynomial on a metric that tracks the real solver,\n and
      it is a SMALL win: the poly is ~0.8% from the smooth-optimal and this closes
      most of it.\n MEASURED (solver elbow err % of arm, in-sample, VALIDATED numpy
      port): BasisArmSwivelModel 3.572%\n -> this 3.543%. The MLP was trained against
      the ported solver + a temporal pop penalty."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
