  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ReprojectInverseOffsetPosition
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 10
    ParamNames:
    - calibUnscaledTrackerPos
    - calibUnscaledTrackerRot
    - calibUnscaledHeadPos
    - calibUnscaledHeadRot
    - deviceScale
    - offsetPos
    - offsetRot
    - headTposeLocalScaled
    - boneTposeLocalScaled
    - trackerRot
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Re-derives a calibrated FBT tracker's POSITION inverse offset for a
      (possibly different) avatar\n and DeviceScale, from scale-free calibration
      snapshots \u2014 the position analog of the rotation\n calibration's reference
      mechanism, and what lets an FBT calibration survive an avatar swap or a\n scale
      change without redoing the T-pose.\n\n Rebuilds the calibration geometry at
      the CURRENT scale: the tracker and head snapshots (unscaled\n device space)
      are re-scaled with ScaleDeviceCoord, the avatar is virtually anchored\n with
      DriveTpose's own math (yaw-flattened head; root placed so the head bone lands
      on the head),\n and the bone reference is that anchored root plus the avatar's
      own T-pose bind\n (TposeLocalScaled, avatar-root-local \u2014 the same quantity
      DriveTpose uses for the head). The\n offset then captures exactly like BasisInput.CalculateOffset
      does against a live T-pose. The\n player's live pose at reprojection time is
      irrelevant."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
