  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: StandingEyeDenominator
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - playerMeasuredHeight
    - eyeReference
    - additionalPlayerHeight
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The DeviceScale denominator: the player's TRUE standing eye height
      in real-world metres -- the\n height the HMD center-eye sits at when standing
      level. DeviceScale divides the avatar's rendered\n eye height by this, so the
      avatar only feels right when this equals the real standing eye height.\n `eyeReference`
      lifts a backend's tracked point up to the eyes: OpenVR fills it\n from SteamVR's
      eye-to-head transform (BasisInput.CenterEyeVerticalOffset) because it tracks
      the\n HMD pose origin, while a backend whose tracked point is already the center-eye
      (OpenXR\n centerEyePosition) passes 0. A shortfall in this denominator is exactly
      what the additive\n `additionalPlayerHeight` term bridges."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ComputeDeviceScale
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - avatarUnscaledMetric
    - appliedUpScale
    - playerMeasuredHeight
    - eyeReference
    - 1e-5f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "DeviceScale: maps real HMD/tracker motion onto the avatar so the rendered
      first-person viewpoint\n lands at the avatar's scaled eye height. Equals (avatarUnscaledMetric
      * appliedUpScale) divided by\n StandingEyeDenominator. Feel is correct iff
      that denominator equals the player's true\n standing eye height E: a denominator
      short by g yields E/(E-g) too-tall and is cancelled by a +g\n nudge; a denominator
      long by g yields the matching too-short. Returns 1 for a degenerate\n (near-zero)
      denominator so a bad measurement can never poison the bones."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
