    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Floor height inferred from the player's own low trackers: the lowest
      tracker, minus the mount\n allowance, provided at least MinFootBandTrackers
      trackers sit together in the foot\n band and the implied eye height (hmd -
      floor) is a plausible human measurement. Because the HMD\n and every tracker
      carry the SAME vertical play-space shift, measuring the eye against this floor\n
      cancels ANY such shift \u2014 the Basis play-space mover, the arm-span grounding
      lift, and offsets\n applied outside Basis (an OVRAS/SteamVR space drag) alike
      \u2014 with no offset bookkeeping at all.\n This is what lets the player calibrate
      wherever they happen to be."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
