    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "As above, plus the two symmetry-breaking inputs the branch needs at
      the top of the circle.\n\n `prevSide` is the side this arm's guard chose last
      frame (-1 / +1), or 0 for \"no history\" -- a\n cold start, a dropout, or a
      frame on which the guard did not fire. `sideUsed` is what to carry\n into next
      frame's `prevSide`; it is 0 whenever the guard declined or was inside its envelope,
      so\n a stale side can never be held across a stretch where the guard was not
      the thing deciding.\n\n `lateralOut` is the body-lateral axis pointing AWAY
      from the torso for this arm (the shoulder\n line, signed by which arm this
      is). It is used ONLY to seed the very first frame inside the tie\n band, where
      there is no history and `sign(s)` is a coin flip that hysteresis would then
      hold.\n\n Zero/0 for either -- the struct defaults -- declines that half, and
      zero for BOTH is bit-identical\n to the pre-band guard."
