    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The bend direction the two-bone solver wants: a UNIT vector PERPENDICULAR
      to the shoulder->hand\n axis. Perpendicular by construction, so it lies on
      the elbow's reachable circle and the solver\n has nothing to project away and
      no near-singular projection to guard.\n\n THE PROJECTION IS THE WHOLE FUNCTION.
      No fade, no blend, no second opinion: blending this\n direction toward any
      fixed pole re-creates the flip (see the file header -- an antipodal lerp\n
      cancels, and its cancellation surface cut through healthy workspace; it is
      also LOUDER under\n noise than the raw projection, 25.5 deg vs 8.1 under 2
      mm of hand jitter). The rest pole enters\n only as normalizesafe's fallback,
      on the measure-zero cores where the projection has no length.\n\n `elbowLocal`
      is this model's prediction, `tipLocal` the hand, both in the mirrored body
      frame.\n `conditioning` comes back as the pole's lever arm in arm lengths --
      a purely GEOMETRIC number\n (how far the predicted elbow stands off the arm's
      own axis), not a regression's opinion of\n itself. It is reported for tests
      and gizmos."
