    Summary: "There IS an established previous choice to stay near. \u26A0\uFE0F
      THIS IS NOT \"the caller has a\n slot to store one in\" -- it must be false
      on the first engaging frame and after any disengage,\n because an anchor seeded
      at zero is not neutral, it is a PULL TOWARD THE NATURAL POLE. At\n k_TemporalAnchorPerDeg
      a 90 deg swing would be priced at 45 mm of clearance, more than a swing\n can
      ever buy, so a zero-seeded anchor suppresses exactly the large swings the full
      circle exists\n to reach. Measured on the 354k-point sweep: conflating the
      two took the cleared fraction the\n WRONG WAY, 0.3606 -> 0.3552, with mean
      swing falling 12.68 -> 11.70 deg. The domain and the\n anchor are independent
      knobs and must stay that way."
