  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: Apply
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 7
    ParamNames:
    - prevBend
    - prevAxis
    - curAxis
    - rawBend
    - maxGain
    - dReach
    - conditioning
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Cap the bend's swivel about the shoulder->hand axis to `maxGain` times
      the hand's\n own motion since last frame -- the axis's rotation PLUS its gated
      radial travel. All vectors WORLD\n space, unit; rawBend and the result are
      perpendicular to curAxis.\n\n prevBend / prevAxis are last frame's CAPPED bend
      and shoulder->hand axis (the caller's per-arm\n state). Away from a core the
      field turns slower than the cap and rawBend is returned unchanged,\n bit-for-bit
      -- so this is a true no-op on ordinary motion.\n\n `dReach` is the change in
      |hand - shoulder| / armLength since prevAxis was\n stored -- the component
      of the hand's motion the axis rotation cannot see, and the one a punch is\n
      made of. Sign is ignored. Pass 0 and this is the rotation-only cap exactly.\n\n
      `conditioning` is the field's own lever arm for this pose (ArmHint's out\n
      parameter, BendDirection's `conditioning`). It gates the radial term ONLY --
      see ReachTrust and\n the file header. Pass 0 and the radial term is off whatever
      dReach says."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
