    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "ROOT-RELATIVE bind of the same bone TposeChestRot is baked from, so
      BasisShoulderSolveCore\n can build its girdle frame anatomically instead of
      reading the chest BONE's local axes as\n lateral/up/forward. Derived from TposeChestRot
      so it can never drift to a different bone than the\n live rotation. Root-relative
      and not the raw world bind: a world bind leaves the anatomical axes\n tilted
      by whatever yaw the AnimatorRoot happened to have at capture -- the same trap\n
      BasisCalibrationDebugCsvWindow already warns about for the head offset. Zero
      declines."
