  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: ApplyToeSurfaceBend
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 4
    ParamNames:
    - stream
    - handle
    - bendDeg
    - 1e-6f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bend the toe about a world medio-lateral axis, on top of wherever the
      pose already has it.\n\n Deliberately RELATIVE, not an absolute target. Reading
      the toe's current world rotation and adding a\n delta is identity at zero bend
      BY CONSTRUCTION, so this cannot come out toes-up the way an absolute\n LookRotation-style
      target did -- that bug cost a whole investigation, and the foot's footAlign\n
      rest-basis map exists solely to undo it. It also needs no calibration offset
      (offsetRotationLeftToe is\n only meaningful when a toe CONTROL was actually
      calibrated, which it is not on the procedural path)\n and no assumption about
      the rig's toe bone axes.\n\n Runs after SolveLegs, so the toe's composed world
      rotation already carries the solved foot.\n Sign: positive bendDeg is DORSIFLEXION
      (toes up). A positive AngleAxis about world-right pitches\n forward toward
      down in Unity's left-handed frame, hence the negation."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
