    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The ARM's body frame, live, from BONE POSITIONS: shoulder line for
      right, chest->neck for up.\n\n From POSITIONS, not from the chest bone's ROTATION,
      and that is the whole reason it transfers. A\n bone's local axes are a rig
      convention, so a frame taken from rotations is fitted to one skeleton and\n
      no other. It also deletes the old frame's entire problem: ArmBendFrame had
      to strip the chest's YAW\n (or head-gaze chest twist swept the lookup and flipped
      the elbow pole) and then spring-smooth the hips\n to stop hip sway wobbling
      the derived elbow. A position frame has no yaw to strip -- the shoulder line\n
      IS the yaw -- so both the twist-extraction and the hip-frame spring go away."
    Remarks: 
