    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Body-frame normal defining ANTERIOR for the knee's half-space guard.
      Zero (the struct\n default) falls back to BendNormal, so every existing caller
      is unchanged.\n\n Split out because BendNormal does double duty -- fallback
      pole AND anterior reference -- and the two\n want different frames. When BendNormal
      rides a lower-leg tracker (FBIKTrackerBendNormal) the guard's\n notion of \"anterior\"
      rotates with the user's SHIN, so ordinary tibial rotation drags a legal knee\n
      into the guard's compression band: measured 41 deg of knee travel from 60 deg
      of tibial rotation on a\n hint that never moved, and the guard engaging at
      only 20 deg. Anterior must stay body-frame; the\n tracker-derived plane is
      still exactly right for the POLE."
    Remarks: 
