  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisLegSwivelNeuralModel
    MemberName: BasisLegSwivelNeuralModel
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: " <summary>\n AUTO-GENERATED by tools/neural_ik/train_swivel.py -- DO
      NOT HAND-EDIT. Re-fit and re-generate.\n\n A neural drop-in for BasisLegSwivelModel.SwivelRad.
      Predicts the knee's swivel angle\n about the hip->foot axis from the SAME mirrored,
      body-frame, limb-normalized tip position, via a small\n MLP (3->24->16->2,
      tanh) whose two outputs are (sin, cos) of the angle. Output convention is IDENTICAL
      to\n BasisLegSwivelModel, so BasisLegSwivelModel.BendDirection consumes it
      unchanged and sqrt(s*s+c*c) is the confidence.\n\n Fitted on the harness's
      OWN dumped features (basis_leg_train.csv);\n fit frame == eval frame. NEVER
      re-derive the features in a different frame -- the twice-burned\n \"confident
      garbage\" trap (a mismatch in handedness/body-frame/mirror scored 3.77% offline,
      31% in-harness).\n\n MEASURED (proxy knee position error, % of limb, held-out
      CLIPS -- generalization):\n     BasisLegSwivelModel (refit)    .. 4.156%\n    
      THIS MODEL ........................ 3.230%   (2.265% in-sample)\n Worst radial
      pole step (smoothness, the accuracy proxy is blind to it): 5.5 deg in-reach,\n
      5.2 deg at the reach boundary, 0 past reach (clamp). Seed picked for accuracy
      AND smoothness.\n Codegen parity (numpy float32 replicate vs torch, max over
      the corpus): 9.16e-05 deg.\n So this C# IS the trained network -- the constants
      below reproduce it to float precision.\n The same domain clamp is load-bearing:
      outside |t|<=1 the fit is void, so the tip is projected\n onto the unit ball
      first, exactly as BasisLegSwivelModel does.\n </summary>"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
