  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisPelvisPostureModel
    MemberName: Coupling
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - drop
    - lean
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "How much of the head's drop the PELVIS should follow. 0 = the pelvis
      stays where it is and the\n spine folds (a waist-bend). 1 = the pelvis rides
      the head straight down (a squat or a sit).\n\n   drop   (standing head height
      - current head height) / standing head height.   >= 0\n   lean   horizontal
      distance from the head to the SUPPORT BASE (the feet, or the standing spot\n         
      when the feet are not tracked), over that same standing head height.   >= 0\n\n
      Both are fractions of the user's own height, so the model is SCALE-FREE: a
      child avatar and a\n giant get the same posture rather than the same centimetres."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
