  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: BuildRestFrame
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - boneWorldPos
    - childWorldPos
    - boneWorldRot
    - parentWorldRot
    - hipsRightWorld
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Build a bone's anatomical rest frame from the T-POSE, using POSITIONS
      for the two axes that\n matter and the bone's own rest rotation only as the
      neutral.\n\n THE AXES COME FROM POSITIONS BECAUSE A BONE'S LOCAL AXES ARE A
      RIG CONVENTION AND DO NOT TRANSFER.\n This project has been bitten by that
      repeatedly -- it is why the arm swivel model is position-only\n and why BasisFootSimParams
      carries a rest-basis map. `up` is the bone's own long axis (joint to\n child);
      `right` is the subject's right, taken from the hips, which is a body-wide fact
      and not a\n property of any one bone. Everything is then expressed in the PARENT's
      rest frame, which is the\n frame the joint's local rotation already lives in.\n\n
      `boneWorld`/`childWorld` are the bone and its next bone down the chain; `parentWorldRot`
      is the\n bone's parent. `hipsRightWorld` is the subject's right, from the hips."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
