  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: OvershootAsymptote
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "How far past the anatomical limit the guard's asymptote sits. The limit
      itself is the SOFT\n threshold -- every anatomically legal pose passes through
      untouched -- and the guard eases from\n there toward `limit * OvershootAsymptote`,
      which it never reaches.\n\n Why tolerate any overshoot at all: published ROM
      has real inter-subject spread (van Arkel's hip\n extension is -12 +/- 7 deg),
      so a hard wall at the population mean would fight a hypermobile user\n on poses
      their own spine makes comfortably. 1.25x is inside that spread and still 2-3x
      tighter\n than what shipped -- which, past the CCD, was no limit at all."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
