  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisSwivelFrame
    MemberName: BasisSwivelFrame
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The body frame the swivel models are fitted in: a right-handed triad
      built from BONE POSITIONS.\n\n From POSITIONS, never from bone rotations. A
      bone's local axes are a RIG CONVENTION -- CMU's chest bone\n is not Unity's
      -- so a frame taken from rotations is fitted to one skeleton and no other.
      A shoulder\n line and a spine direction are ANATOMY, and anatomy transfers
      between rigs.\n\n `Right` is the UN-MIRRORED body right. The mirror (+x OUTWARD
      for both limbs, so that one model serves\n both) is applied per-limb in Features()."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
