  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisSwivelHintCore
    MemberName: LegDomainReachLo
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Reach (|tipLocal|, foot distance / leg length) below which the swivel
      model is outside its fit\n domain and its OWN confidence stops protecting anyone.
      Measured on the deep-crouch descent\n (foot under the hip, leg folding toward
      the heels): as reach falls through ~0.45 the predicted\n swivel walks from
      +85 (knee forward, right) to -48 (knee inward-backward, garbage) while the\n
      confidence dips to 0.28 and then RECOVERS to 0.86 inside the garbage zone --
      confidently wrong,\n so the |(s,c)| trust gate re-trusts it, the anterior half-space
      guard then catches the posterior\n pole and pins BOTH knees dead-lateral at
      ~88 deg: the \"legs go 180 out to the sides\" crouch bug,\n with 30-38 mm/frame
      clicks on the way in. CMU simply has no frames with the foot under the hip\n
      at fractional reach (a human squat keeps the heels forward of the pelvis),
      so out there the\n polynomial is an RNG with a good poker face.\n\n Below LegDomainReachLo
      the model's opinion is discarded outright: trust goes to zero and the\n pole
      eases onto the solver's anatomical BendNormal pole (sagittal, knees over the
      toes) through\n the existing HintDistrust path -- which is exactly right for
      every real pose down there\n (deep squat on the heels, kneeling, sitting on
      heels: the knee points FORWARD). At or above\n LegDomainReachHi this is exactly
      1, so every fitted pose is bit-for-bit unchanged (a full-depth\n crouch with
      the sit-back engaged solves at reach ~0.66)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
