    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "How far to trust BasisLegSwivelModel, read off its own |(s,c)|.\n\n
      The magnitude is the model's opinion STRENGTH, and the domain clamp in SwivelRad
      bounds the\n radius but cannot bound the DIRECTION \u2014 so leg ABDUCTION
      (standing with the feet apart) walks\n straight out of a fit whose corpus is
      CMU walk/idle/reach/sit. Measured on a 22\xB0 abduction:\n confidence 0.98
      \u2192 0.28 while the predicted swivel runs 4\xB0 \u2192 70\xB0, rotating the
      knee out of the\n sagittal plane and back inward. Out there the answer is not
      approximate, it is invented.\n\n Smoothstep so the pole it feeds is C1 and
      cannot kink."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
