    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Where the KNEE goes with no knee tracker. Same shape as ArmHint, three
      differences, all measured:\n\n   * the frame hangs off the PELVIS (hip line,
      hips->chest), not the chest;\n   * the swivel's reference is body OUTWARD and
      is passed MIRRORED (the arm's is body-down and is not);\n   * NO confidence
      gate. Fading the hint weight toward zero does not avoid a pop, it CREATES one
      --\n     the knee falls back to the solver's BendNormal pole, which points
      somewhere unrelated, and\n     swinging between two unrelated poles over a
      few frames IS a pop. Measured: the fade took the knee\n     from 70 pops to
      65. It relocated the discontinuity, it did not remove it."
    Remarks: 
