  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.
    MemberName: ExtractYawBurst
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - rotation
    - 1e-12f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Yaw deadzone for the torso: holds the chest/spine/hips heading at an
      anchor until the head\n leaves the cone, then eases a 0..1 follow weight in
      so the chain blends into the catch-up\n (and back out) instead of snapping
      at the edge. Re-centers the anchor once fully engaged and\n the head stops,
      so reversing has to re-cross the cone. While locomoting the cone is bypassed\n
      so the torso re-aligns to the head. Head and neck are unaffected."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
