  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.BasisBodyFitNetworking
    MemberName: BasisBodyFitNetworking
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Networks the local player's body fit (per-segment arm/leg/torso scales;
      see BasisBodyFitCore) so\n remotes render the wearer at their calibrated proportions
      instead of the avatar's authored ones.\n\n It rides AvatarChangeMessageChannel
      under a kind discriminator rather than a channel of its own \u2014\n all 64
      LiteNetLib channels are assigned, and that channel already has the two properties
      this\n needs: the server stores the record per player and replays it to late
      joiners. So this class only\n has to do change detection on the way out and
      application on the way in; it deliberately does NOT\n re-broadcast to newly
      seen players the way the older spine-proportion networking had to, because\n
      the server is now the one answering joiners."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
