  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Debugging.
    MemberName: Action
    Kind: Event
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Identify colours, in pick order. Two constraints the old palette missed:\n\n
      Red and green sat at indices 0 and 1, so the first two trackers a user\n identified
      \u2014 in full body, almost always the two feet \u2014 came out in the\n one
      pair of hues red-green colourblindness cannot separate (~8% of men).\n Blue
      and orange lead here instead: that pair survives every common form\n of colour
      blindness, and the rest are spread so the early picks stay far\n apart in hue
      AND in brightness, which is the only cue left to someone who\n sees no hue
      at all.\n\n Every entry also has to read against the dark menu background (palette\n
      BackgroundColor1, ~0.1 luma) as small text, and survive being multiplied\n
      by EmissionIntensity into an emissive sphere in-world."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
