  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.BasisTrackingHardwareClassifier
    MemberName: Refine
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 4
    ParamNames:
    - assumed
    - commonDeviceIdentifier
    - deviceSerial
    - StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "SlimeVR stamps the body part into the serial (\"human://WAIST\"). Both
      of its delivery paths\n do it \u2014 the SolarXR source and the virtual SteamVR
      trackers its driver publishes \u2014 so this\n single test catches SlimeVR
      whether it announces itself as its own subsystem or arrives\n disguised as
      an ordinary OpenVR tracker. Without it, IMU trackers inherit OpenVR's\n lighthouse
      assumption and get filtered far too lightly, which is exactly the buzz they
      need\n smoothing for. Kept in sync with BasisSlimeVRTrackerRoles.SerialPrefix,
      which cannot be\n referenced from here (the OpenVR package must not depend
      on the SlimeVR integration)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
