  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisArmSolveRecorder
    MemberName: ChainAxialEnvelopeDeg
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The envelope BasisArmDiagnostics.ChainAxialDeg is FLAGGED against --
      flagged,\n never gated, and never used to change the solve.\n\n Anatomical
      forearm pronation/supination is ~80 deg each way from the thumbs-up neutral,
      which is\n already this codebase's own number (BasisArmSolveCore.WristRollComfortDeg
      = 80). The radiocarpal\n joint has essentially NO independent axial degree
      of freedom, so the chain total past the\n humerus should not meaningfully exceed
      the forearm's own arc. 90 is that 80 plus a 10 deg\n allowance for an arbitrary
      rig's bind neutral not sitting exactly at anatomical neutral.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F
      IT IS A REPORTING THRESHOLD AND NOTHING ELSE. The whole point of a user capture
      is that we do\n not currently know what this number should be; a breach count
      is a QUESTION raised, not a defect\n proven. Read it next to the occupied-arc
      percentiles for the same cell."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
