  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.
    MemberName: Stop
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 0
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Ends the session and releases everything without printing. Safe at
      any time.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F IT CLEARS THE STATISTICS AS WELL AS THE WRITER,
      AND THAT IS NOT TIDINESS. A stopped recorder\n that still answers CapturedFrames,
      RowsWritten and Summary() from the LAST session reports stale\n numbers as
      current ones -- and a stale segmented table is the single most misleading artifact\n
      this instrument could produce, because it is indistinguishable from a fresh
      one. Caught by\n BasisArmSolveRecorderTests: a gated-off Begin reported 300
      rows it had not written, and an empty\n session summarised as the previous
      4000-frame capture.\n\n StopAndDump takes its summary BEFORE calling this,
      so nothing is lost. LastWrittenPath\n deliberately survives: it names the file
      on disk, which outlives the session by design."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
