    Summary: "Headless audio clip player for stress testing. Loads .wav or .opus
      files from a directory,\n picks one randomly, Opus-encodes it, and sends it
      over the network as voice audio.\n Self-contained: has its own Opus encoder
      and sends directly via the network peer.\n\n Place .wav or .opus files in:
      {Application.dataPath}/AudioClips/\n If the directory is missing or empty,
      no audio is sent (silent headless as usual).\n\n Designed for testing what
      1000+ simultaneous audio sources sound and look like.\n Each headless client
      picks a random clip and loops it over the network."
