  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.
    MemberName: ComputeFollowLocalPose
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 6
    ParamNames:
    - recordedScaledPosition
    - recordedScaledRotation
    - replayOffsetPosition
    - replayOffsetRotation
    - localPosition
    - localRotation
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Inverts Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.Simulation.BasisInputXRSimulate.LateDoPollData's\n
      forward map, so a simulated device fed this local pose republishes EXACTLY
      the recorded scaled pose.\n\n The simulated device computes, from its FollowMovement
      local pose:\n     ScaledDeviceCoord.position = OffsetCoords.position + (OffsetCoords.rotation
      * localPos)\n     ScaledDeviceCoord.rotation = OffsetCoords.rotation * localRot\n
      so the inverse is a single rigid un-transform. Crucially this is solved against
      the REPLAY-TIME\n OffsetCoords, not the recorded one: OffsetCoords is a process-global
      on BasisInput that the\n playspace mover and calibration both write, so it
      will not generally match the recording. Solving\n against the live value makes
      the replayed scaled pose immune to that drift, which is the whole\n reason
      the recorder stores the scaled pose as the primary signal rather than the raw
      one.\n\n This is also why Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.Simulation.BasisInputXRSimulate.AccountForScale\n
      must stay false on a replay device: it multiplies ScaledDeviceCoord by a second
      scale factor\n after this map, and there is no inverse for it here."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
