  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisDeviceStreamRecorder
    MemberName: BasisDeviceStreamRecorder
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Developer-only recorder that turns a REAL headset session into permanent,
      replayable test data.\n\n This is the unified DEVICE-LEVEL recorder. The four
      recorders that already exist each capture one\n subsystem's output \u2014 BasisCalibrationDebugRecorder
      (calibration stages),\n BasisArmIKRuntimeRecorder (solved arm chain), BasisPairingRotationRecorder\n
      (linked-pair hip fusion) and BasisFootIKDiagnostics (foot plant/slide). All
      four record what the IK\n PRODUCED, in CSV, for a human to read. This one records
      what the IK was GIVEN, in binary, for a\n machine to replay. That makes it
      complementary rather than a replacement: none of the four is made\n redundant,
      but all four become reproducible, because their input can now be re-fed frame
      for frame.\n\n Gating follows BasisCalibrationDebugRecorder's precedent exactly:
      the toggle is read\n ONCE at Begin, and while off every Sample call is a single
      bool test, so the\n instrumentation is free to leave wired in. Output lands
      under persistentDataPath/DeviceStream,\n matching the CalibrationDebug / ArmIKRuntime
      / PairingRotation convention.\n\n WHAT IS CAPTURED, and why each part is not
      optional:\n   - per frame, per device: role, unscaled + scaled pose, connected
      flag, and the frame's timestep;\n   - once per session: the full calibration
      block and every device's calibration residual.\n The calibration is mandatory
      because the same device stream against a different calibration is a\n different
      input. A recording without it would replay, look plausible, and mean nothing."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisDeviceStreamRecorder
    MemberName: DeveloperEnabled
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Developer gate. FALSE BY DEFAULT and must stay that way \u2014 this
      writes megabytes per minute.\n\n This is currently a plain static rather than
      a settings binding because adding one requires\n editing BasisSettingsDefaults,
      which this change does not touch. The intended wiring is a\n sibling of DumpCalibrationCsv:\n    
      public static BasisSettingsBinding<bool> DumpDeviceStreamRecording =\n        
      new(\"devdumpdevicestream\", new BasisPlatformDefault<bool>(false));\n read
      here in Begin the way DumpCalibrationCsv is read in\n BasisCalibrationDebugRecorder.Begin.
      Until then a developer sets this from a debug menu or the\n console before
      calling Begin."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
