  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisFootRotationDebug
    MemberName: BasisFootRotationDebug
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Runtime diagnostic for the foot-IK target rotation. The correct foot
      orientation is the bone-sim\n WORLD foot (OutgoingWorldData) -- it's the animation/standing
      foot and is valid every frame, independent\n of the FBIK. So this logs, per
      foot per frame, how far the rendered foot is from that correct foot\n (the
      bug magnitude), and for each candidate target rotation how far (candidate*offset)
      lands from the\n correct foot -- i.e. which target, when fed, makes finalFoot
      = the correct foot. Measure on foot-IK-ON\n frames (stand still). Stop+Dump
      writes a CSV + a PASS/FAIL summary naming the target to feed."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisLegCrouchDebug
    MemberName: BasisLegCrouchDebug
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Runtime diagnostic for the leg/knee during crouch. Logs, per leg per
      frame, the leg-IK inputs (hip,\n foot target, knee hint) and the rendered knee,
      plus the \"shoot up\" signals: knee above the hip and the\n knee's per-frame
      position jump. Crouch up/down in VR, then Stop+Dump to see the exact inputs
      at the\n frame the leg flips -- crucially this includes the LIVE foot-driver
      knee hint, which the offline crouch\n sweep (synthetic hint) can't reproduce."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisLegSwivelDebug
    MemberName: BasisLegSwivelDebug
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Runtime diagnostic for the knee SWIVEL, per leg per frame. Built to
      answer one question: when one knee\n misbehaves and the other is fine, WHICH
      input differs? The solve path is mirror-symmetric (same\n KneeAnteriorRef,
      same captured bend normal, mirrored driver blocks, and an ODD anterior clamp),
      so a\n left/right asymmetry has to come from the DATA, and this is what reads
      the data.\n\n Rows are Basis.IK.BasisLegDiagnostics verbatim -- its own Header/ToRow,
      not a second copy\n of the field list, so the two cannot drift.\n\n The column
      that is NOT in the diagnostics struct is bendVsAnt: the angle between that
      leg's BendNormal\n (which rides the lower-leg TRACKER when FBIKTrackerBendNormal
      is on) and KneeAnteriorRef (which is always\n body-frame hips-right). Those
      two frames are what the anterior guard and the pole eases are measured\n against
      respectively, and the guard-first ordering in BasisLegSolveCore only keeps
      the near-colinear\n slerp well-conditioned while they agree to within ~90 deg
      -- measured 1.3x knee gain up to 90, then 316x\n at 120 and 471x at 180. A
      strap rotated on one shin, or a stale bend-normal capture, shows up here as
      a\n large bendVsAnt on that leg alone.\n\n Read the SUMMARY first; the CSV
      is for the frame the number goes bad."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
