  - TypeFullName: BasisLocalHandDriver
    MemberName: BasisLocalHandDriver
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Drives per-finger poses for both hands. Bakes a 2D pose grid at init
      time,\n then each frame schedules one Burst job: BasisFingerSlerpJob interpolates
      each joint's target from the\n grid, slerps toward it and writes the transform.
      It was two chained jobs until the dependency fence and\n the second dispatch
      turned out to cost far more than the ~3 us of work in the whole chain.\n Follows
      the Simulate/Apply pattern used by BasisPickupSyncDriver and JigglePhysics.\n\n
      Pose grid data is cached per humanoid Avatar asset. Loading the same avatar
      a second\n time copies from cache instead of re-instantiating and sampling
      441 poses."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
