  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisLocalRigDriver
    MemberName: LeftHandIKOffset
    Kind: Property
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The FBIK hand target offsets (landmark frame -> hand bone frame), as
      plain quaternions.\n\n MediaPipe needs these to cancel FBIK's offset -- it
      emits an already-finished BONE rotation, so the\n solve's own `target * offset`
      would apply the palm->bone map a second time. But BasisFullBodyIK derives\n
      from RigConstraint<,,>, so reading `.data` from another package forces com.basis.mediapipe
      to take a hard\n dependency on Unity.Animation.Rigging just to fetch two quaternions.
      Handing them out from here -- inside\n the assembly that already references
      Rigging -- keeps that dependency where it belongs.\n\n Identity when there
      is no constraint yet, which is the correct no-op: an uncalibrated offset must
      not\n rotate anything."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
