  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ScheduleSurfaceProbes
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - DiscardPendingProbes(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Conform one PLANTED foot to the surface under it: four downward probes
      (heel, two at the ball, one at the\n toe tip) give a fitted ground plane for
      the foot's pitch and roll, plus a separate toe-tip sample that\n articulates
      the toe over a break in the surface.\n\n Why this exists: filteredNormal was
      written at exactly three places -- plant, re-snap and init -- so a\n PLANTED
      foot never re-sampled the ground. Walk onto a slope and the foot kept whatever
      normal it happened\n to plant with; the alignment machinery in BuildFootFrame/FootRotation
      was fully built but starved.\n\n The plane is fitted from HEEL->BALL only,
      deliberately excluding the toe: the toe is the part that is\n allowed to articulate,
      so including it would let a rise under the toe tilt the whole rigid foot instead\n
      of bending the joint that exists for it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
