  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.BasisBalanceSummary
    MemberName: ComHeightFracStature
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The SAME height as a fraction of estimated STATURE, which is the form
      the literature\n states and therefore the one that can be checked against it
      rather than against ourselves. Stature\n is inferred from a different Winter
      row than the mass table (greater trochanter 0.530H, ankle\n 0.039H, so the
      hip-to-ankle span this skeleton measures is 0.491H) -- so agreement with Dempster's\n
      0.553 is an INDEPENDENT confirmation of the segment masses, not a restatement
      of them.\n Measured across the corpus: 0.544 root, 0.539 posture, 0.551 dynamic,
      0.547 slow."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
