      at the wrist rather\n than half a hand further on. The hand is 0.6% of body
      mass over a ~9 cm lever, so the whole-body CoM\n error this costs is bounded
      by 0.6 mm per hand -- stated as a bound rather than hand-waved, because\n an
      unbounded approximation in a mass model is how a metric starts lying."
