    Summary: "One foot's ground footprint: a rectangle from the heel to the toe tip,
      laid along the foot's own\n horizontal axis. Its LENGTH is taken from the projected
      ankle->MTP vector rather than the rigid bone,\n so a pitched foot (heel up
      in push-off) correctly reports a shorter footprint; its WIDTH is taken\n from
      the rigid foot length, because a foot does not get narrower when it tilts."
