    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Signed distance from a point to a CONVEX polygon: positive inside (distance
      to the nearest edge),\n negative outside (distance to the nearest edge segment).
      Orientation is read from the polygon's own\n signed area rather than assumed,
      so a hull built in either winding gives the same answer -- an\n assumed winding
      is the kind of thing that silently inverts a metric."
