  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.BasisBodyPlausibility
    MemberName: TorsoCoreFracHipWidth
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Torso core radius as a fraction of hip-socket width. 0.42 of a ~0.18
      m hip width is ~0.076 m.\n\n THE BINDING CASE IS AN ELBOW TUCKED TO THE STERNUM,
      not an arm through the chest. A real tucked\n elbow's axis sits ~0.11-0.13
      m from the spine; the upper arm's own core radius is ~0.022, so the\n torso
      may not exceed ~0.09 without calling that pose a collision. 0.076 leaves ~0.013
      m of margin\n there and still reports ~0.08 m of penetration for a forearm
      driven through the sternum, which is\n the separation this layer has to be
      able to tell apart."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
