    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Arm / leg core radius as a fraction of that segment's own length --
      roughly half the flesh radius\n (a 0.25 m forearm gets 0.020 m; a 0.44 m thigh
      gets 0.035 m).\n\n THE BINDING CASE IS STANDING WITH THE ARMS DOWN: the forearm's
      axis runs ~0.085 m outboard of the\n femur's, and those two radii sum to ~0.055,
      so the tightest legal pose in the whole body still has\n ~35% headroom. That
      pair is the one to watch first if the corpus ever reports a false positive."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
