  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.BasisBodyPlausibility
    MemberName: MaxPenetrationFracLimb
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Deepest single overlap allowed, as a fraction of the shorter segment's
      length. This is the GROSS\n gate: a forearm driven through the sternum reports
      0.3192, a limb merely brushing another reports\n a few hundredths. The rate
      gate above is the sensitive one; this one exists so a single\n catastrophic
      frame fails even in a long clip where the rate stays low.\n\n \u2B50 NO LONGER
      A GUESS. Measured 2026-07-22 over all 109 clips / 133,078 frames, the worst
      depth\n real human motion produces on a DEPTH-DISCRIMINATING pair is 0.125
      (torso x R-upperarm,\n root/141_17 f5). The synthetic arm-through-sternum fixture
      produces 0.3192. So 0.20 sits 1.60x\n above anything a real human did and 0.63x
      below an unambiguous pass-through -- headroom on both\n sides, which is what
      a threshold is supposed to have. It is UNCHANGED in value; what changed is\n
      that Gate() now applies it only where depth discriminates (PairDepthDiscriminating),
      because the\n arm x same-side-leg family saturates its depth number on real
      motion and was failing 8 of the 109\n clips before that scope fix."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
