  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.
    MemberName: BuildSpineRest
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - StraightestFrame(c
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Capture the three spine rest frames at the subject's straightest frame
      -- the clip's own\n anatomical neutral, which is what makes every spine angle
      a deviation FROM rest rather than a\n deviation from whatever the rig happened
      to author. Same reference-finding rule as\n BasisSpineAnatomyCorpusTests, and
      the same shipping BuildRestFrame.\n\n THE UPPER THORACIC IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT.
      In the CMU skeleton `Neck` sits at ZERO offset from\n `Spine1` (the upper-chest
      joint) -- they are the same point -- so UpperChest has no measurable\n long
      axis in this corpus, and routing the axis up through the coincident neck instead
      reads a\n phantom ~27 deg of flexion. That is a property of the corpus, not
      of the segment; a real avatar\n has a genuine upperChest->neck length and measures
      fine at runtime."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
