    Summary: "Minimum distance between two line SEGMENTS, with the closest points
      clamped to the segments.\n The textbook construction (Ericson, Real-Time Collision
      Detection): solve the unconstrained\n least-squares for the two parameters,
      clamp one, re-solve the other, clamp again. The clamping is\n not a nicety
      -- unclamped, two nearly-parallel bones produce parameters far outside [0,1]
      and the\n reported \"distance\" is between points that are not on either bone."
