    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The humanoid parent of each joint, in BasisMocapJoint's own indexing.
      Reconstructed from the CMU\n hierarchy BasisBvhLoader maps (Hips -> LowerBack
      -> Spine -> Spine1 -> Neck -> Head, with\n Spine1 -> LeftShoulder -> LeftArm
      -> LeftForeArm -> LeftHand and Hips -> LeftUpLeg -> ...);\n CMU's LHipJoint
      / RHipJoint / Neck1 are structural in-betweens that the loader does not map,
      so\n the bone recorded here spans them. That is exactly right for a proportion
      rescale: it is the\n MAPPED joint-to-joint offset that determines the limb
      lengths the solver reads back.\n\n BasisMocapJoint.Count marks a root (only
      the hips)."
    Remarks: 
