    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Every parent must sit EARLIER in BasisMocapJoint than its child, because
      the rebuild is a single\n forward pass that reads delta[parent] before writing
      delta[child]. It holds today by the enum's\n own ordering; a future reorder
      would silently produce a skeleton assembled against stale\n displacements,
      which would look like plausible motion and be wrong. Cheap to check, so it
      is\n checked rather than assumed."
    Remarks: 
