  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.BasisMocapAccuracy
    MemberName: s_swivelDump
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Training-data dump: the EXACT features this harness feeds BasisArmSwivelModel,
      plus the true\n swivel it should have predicted, plus the circle radius (the
      weight).\n\n This exists because fitting in a Python pipeline and evaluating
      in this one is a bug factory: the\n two must agree on the handedness conversion,
      the body frame, the joint mapping and the left/right\n mirror, and a mismatch
      in ANY of them silently poisons the model. The first attempt did exactly\n
      that -- it scored 31% here and 3.77% in Python, and the probe showed the predicted
      swivel was\n 145 degrees off, i.e. the model was being asked about a different
      frame than it was fitted in.\n\n Dumping from HERE and fitting on THAT makes
      the question unaskable: the model is fitted to the\n literal inputs the runtime
      produces. Whatever the conventions are, both sides now share them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
