  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.BasisMocapTracks
    MemberName: BasisMocapTracks
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Per-frame joint tracks from a mocap run: what the human's joint did,
      and what the solver's did,\n frame by frame, in the same units.\n\n The accuracy
      layer above reduces those two tracks to a distance. That answers \"is the pose\n
      right\" and is deliberately blind to \"is the MOTION right\" -- a solved elbow
      can sit 2 cm from\n the truth on every single frame while buzzing at 30 Hz,
      plateauing, or arriving 150 ms late,\n and the mean error will not budge. Handing
      the raw tracks out lets BasisMocapMotionQuality\n score the thing the distance
      throws away.\n\n Left side only, matching the side the ElbowPops/KneePops detectors
      already sample."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
