    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The elbow HINT the lookup path hands the solver, captured at two stages
      so the noise\n can be localised instead of guessed at. HintRaw is the lookup
      table's own output; HintFlared is\n that same bend after BasisElbowFlareCore.ApplyChickenWingFlare,
      which is what actually reaches\n the solver. Comparing their jitter says immediately
      WHICH stage invents the buzz -- the table,\n the flare, or (if both are clean)
      the two-bone solve amplifying a clean hint.\n Populated only when hint == Lookup.
      Left side."
