    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "This is the SAME sample as last frame: the device did not deliver a
      new one and the previous one is\n being held. A hold, never an interpolation,
      because a hold is what actually reaches the solver.\n\n Deliberately NOT \"this
      sample is old\". Latency alone makes every sample old while still delivering
      a\n NEW one each frame, and the two have completely different consequences:
      a delayed-but-moving input\n costs the solver phase, a repeated input costs
      it a velocity of zero followed by a step. Read AgeS\n for the former and this
      for the latter."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
