    Summary: "Everything that stands between the bone and what the solver is handed.
      Every field is neutral at zero,\n and a wholly-zero params is a BIT-EXACT identity
      -- each stage is skipped rather than multiplied by\n zero, so no float rounding
      can creep in. That is what lets a realistic-tracker row be A/B'd against an\n
      existing baseline without re-basing the baseline."
    Remarks: 
