  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Mocap.
    MemberName: DeviceTiming
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - device
    - rateHz
    - (device
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Update rate and delivery latency per device class.\n\n \u26A0 THESE
      ARE ESTIMATES. Unlike the mount and noise numbers -- which are carried across
      from models\n already calibrated in this repo -- nothing here has been measured
      against a real device by this\n project. The RATES are well known (HMD ~90
      Hz, OpenVR pucks ~250 Hz, SlimeVR ~100 Hz); the\n LATENCIES are plausible order-of-magnitude
      figures and are the least trustworthy constants in this\n file. Replace them
      the moment a capture exists, and do not quote a result that turns on them\n
      without saying so."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
