  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Motion.BasisMocapMotionSummary
    MemberName: ElbowPopsInvented
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 POPS THE SOLVER ACTUALLY INVENTED: frames where OUR joint popped
      and the HUMAN'S DID NOT.\n\n This is what *PopExcess above was always meant
      to mean and does not. PopExcess subtracts COUNTS, so\n it cannot tell \"popped
      on the same frames the human did\" (invented nothing) from \"popped the same\n
      number of times, somewhere else entirely\" (invented all of them). Measured
      on the corpus, 69% of the\n knee's flagged frames are frames where the HUMAN'S
      OWN knee jumps too -- a fast motion, a foot\n plant, or the BVH's own rest-to-motion
      discontinuity on frame 1, which is worth a quarter of a metre\n in a single
      step and lands in BOTH tracks. The solver was being charged for the corpus's
      noise."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
