  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Motion.BasisMocapMotionQuality
    MemberName: ReportOnlyShapeDistance
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0 REPORTED, NOT GATED -- deliberately.\n\n Spectral shape distance
      is an excellent DEGRADATION detector (over-smoothing 0.160 vs added\n jitter
      0.001, measured on identical source motion) and it is genuinely informative
      here: on the\n buzzy clips it separates the three hint sources cleanly (69_70:
      Lookup 0.494, None 0.130,\n TruthJoint 0.000). But as an ABSOLUTE cross-trajectory
      gate it is not yet trustworthy: on 02_01\n it scores the TRUE elbow (0.662)
      as moving less like the human than a crude lookup guess (0.568),\n which is
      impossible. Every other clip in the corpus puts TruthJoint at 0.000-0.058,
      so the metric\n is right 19 times out of 20 and I do not understand the twentieth.\n\n
      The suspicion is band-edge sensitivity: with 5 hard-edged bands, a narrowband
      motion sitting near\n a boundary can dump its energy across the edge under
      a small trajectory change. Overlapping or\n smoothly-weighted bands would likely
      fix it.\n\n A metric I cannot explain does not get to fail builds. HintSources_Compared_ForMotionQuality\n
      exists to keep this honest and is currently what is telling us not to trust
      it -- exactly its job.\n Understand the 02_01 case, then promote this back
      to a gate."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
