  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Motion.BasisMotionQuality
    MemberName: PopMinFracLimb
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "...AND it must actually be big enough to SEE. A pop must clear this
      fraction of the limb length in\n a single frame, as well as clearing PopRatio.\n\n
      \u26A0 THE RATIO ALONE IS A LIAR, AND IT WAS LYING. It is scale-RELATIVE, so
      a joint that barely moves has\n a near-zero median and ordinary motion sails
      past 8x. Measured on the corpus (BasisKneePopLocaliser):\n of the knee's 170
      flagged frames, 27 sat on tracks whose median step was under a thousandth of
      a leg,\n where the denominator has collapsed and the metric is measuring nothing
      but its own noise floor. That\n is how the knee scored an identical \"36 excess
      pops\" whether it was handed no hint at all, the old\n lookup, or the fitted
      model -- a number that does not move when its supposed cause moves was never\n
      measuring that cause.\n\n 1% of a limb in ONE frame is ~1.2 limb-lengths/second
      of instantaneous speed at 120 Hz: that is a\n discontinuity. Below it there
      is nothing a user could see, so there is nothing to count. The teleport\n BasisMotionAnalyzerTests
      plants is 13% of its limb and still trips this comfortably."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
