  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Motion.BasisMotionSpectrum
    MemberName: BasisMotionSpectrum
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Frequency-domain metrics for the IK motion-quality harness.\n\n There
      IS an FFT in the repo already (com.basis.openlipsync FFTProcessor) but it is
      `internal`\n to an assembly the IK tests do not reference, so reaching it would
      mean an InternalsVisibleTo\n plus a new asmdef edge to a lipsync package. Not
      worth the coupling for 60 lines of radix-2.\n\n Why the spectrum earns its
      place, when jerk and SPARC already exist: they are SCALARS, and a\n scalar
      cannot tell you WHERE the badness is. The spectrum can. A peak parked at Nyquist
      means\n a two-frame limit cycle (a feedback loop oscillating against itself);
      a peak at the step\n frequency means the stepper; broadband hash means the
      input. Same \"the elbow is jittery\"\n complaint, three completely different
      bugs, and the dominant frequency tells them apart."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
