    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "One-sided power spectrum of a real signal, Hann-windowed and mean-removed.\n\n
      The window is not optional. Without it a non-periodic signal (every joint path
      -- it does\n not start and end in the same place) produces a step discontinuity
      at the DFT wrap-around,\n and the leakage from that step lands in EVERY bin,
      including the high ones we are about to\n call \"jitter\". First attempt at
      this measured the leakage and called it a defect."
