  - TypeFullName: BasisRemoteInterpolationCore
    MemberName: BasisRemoteInterpolationCore
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pure, Burst-friendly interpolation math for remote-avatar playback.\n\n
      Replaces the old linear-nlerp + heavy 1\u20AC bone filter with a C1-continuous\n
      Catmull-Rom spline through four consecutive network snapshots (p0..p3),\n evaluated
      for the segment p1->p2. C1 continuity removes the per-snapshot\n velocity corner
      that linear interpolation produced (the source of the\n end-of-chain wobble),
      without the group delay / amplitude loss the filter\n introduced.\n\n p0 and
      p3 are the neighbours of the active window; the caller supplies them\n from
      the retained previous frame and a peek at the next staged frame. When a\n neighbour
      is unavailable (startup / underrun after loss) the caller passes a\n DUPLICATED
      endpoint (p0==p1 or p3==p2); the tangents then become one-sided\n and the curve
      stays bounded and monotone \u2014 no branch or validity flag needed.\n\n No
      Unity references beyond Unity.Mathematics, so this is unit-testable off the\n
      main thread and reproducible in an offline harness."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
