  - TypeFullName: BasisRemoteLimbIK
    MemberName: BasisRemoteLimbIK
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pure analytic two-bone IK for remote-avatar end-effector anchoring.\n\n
      The remote skeleton is posed by forward kinematics off the interpolated hips,
      so a hand/foot at\n the end of a chain accumulates every joint's error and
      drifts. When the sender marks an effector\n \"anchored\" (a held controller/tracker
      or a planted foot) it ships the tip's WORLD target; the\n receiver then bends
      that one limb so the tip lands exactly on the target, taking its pole hint
      from\n the FK joint rather than a networked swivel angle.\n\n The solve AIMS
      the current FK bones with minimal rotations (no avatar-specific bind-pose axes\n
      needed): rotate the upper bone so the joint reaches the analytic elbow/knee
      position, then rotate\n the lower bone so the tip reaches the target. Result
      is exact (tip == target, joint == the\n law-of-cosines point on the swivel
      circle). Burst-friendly, no Unity refs beyond Unity.Mathematics."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
