  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Sync.
    MemberName: KeyframeBackoffInterval
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - baseInterval
    - idleCount
    - shift
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Keyframe interval stretched by an idle backoff: after `idleCount` consecutive
      keyframes\n with nothing changed, the interval is doubled each step (capped
      at 2^`maxShift`\xD7). A\n late-joiner still gets an immediate keyframe (OnPlayerJoined
      forces one) and any change resets the\n backoff, so recovery cadence is unchanged
      for moving objects \u2014 only idle objects stop re-sending."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
