  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Players.BasisRemotePlayer
    MemberName: BasisRemotePlayer
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IBasisPlayer
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Remote (non-local) player representation used by the Basis SDK.\n Handles
      avatar creation/loading, remote eye/bone driving, network pose consumption,\n
      mesh LOD adjustments, and remote name plate lifecycle."
    Remarks: "Unlike the local player, this is a plain managed object (not a MonoBehaviour)\n
      with no dedicated root GameObject. The avatar, nameplate, and mouth marker
      are each\n independent scene roots positioned by the bone job system, so their
      transform writes\n spread across worker threads. Because it is not a UnityEngine.Object,
      lifecycle is\n explicit: the disconnect path calls OnDestroy to release the
      nameplate and\n mouth (the avatar is unloaded separately by the avatar factory)."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
