    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: HardHintRotations_OnlyHappenInsideTheZeroCores
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Frame(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The two zero cores are REQUIRED to exist (total index 2), but they
      must stay CONFINED: any step\n that does rotate the hint hard must sit at a
      collapsed lever, i.e. inside a core -- never out in\n workspace the model is
      confident about. On the faded model 4-7 hard steps per reach shell sat at\n
      levers of 0.05-0.07; here every one must be under 0.02, and there must be FEW
      of them in total\n (the cores subtend ~2 degrees; a fat count means a new singular
      structure has crept in)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
