  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: Elevation_IsMeasuredInTheTorsoFrame_AndSaysSoWhenItIsNot
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisArmNet.DefaultRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 ELEVATION IS A TORSO QUANTITY. MEASURING IT AGAINST THE PLAYER
      ROOT IS THE DEFECT THAT MADE A\n GUARD FIRE ON ORDINARY BENT-OVER POSES WITH
      ITS MEASUREMENT'S SIGN FLIPPED.\n\n PlayerUp stays vertical while the chest
      does not, so \"above the shoulder\" stops meaning anything\n the moment the
      user bends at the waist. The same is true of every band this capture segments
      by:\n an elevation measured against the root files a bent-over reach into the
      wrong cell, and the cell\n is the unit of the whole analysis.\n\n The mutant
      is the input itself: zeroing TorsoUp is exactly what a rig that cannot build
      a body\n frame sends, and the core documents that as the PlayerUp fallback.
      So this asserts the fed case\n tracks the torso, the declined case does not,
      and TorsoUpValid tells them apart -- because a row\n measured in the fallback
      frame has to be segmented OUT, not pooled in."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
