  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ChainAxial_IsComposed_NotTheSumOfItsJunctions
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F TWISTS ABOUT A COMMON AXIS ONLY ADD THROUGH PURE TWISTS,
      AND THE FOREARM SITS OFF THE\n HUMERUS AT EVERY REAL FLEXION.\n\n The obvious
      implementation of the chain total is ElbowAxialDeg + WristAxialDeg, and it
      is wrong.\n The existing seam-snap test measured the sum form carrying 0.46
      deg of error at a 170 deg elbow\n -- enough to blur an identity gate -- and
      the error grows as the elbow bends. So the capture\n computes the chain total
      COMPOSITIONALLY, and this test proves the two are genuinely different\n things
      rather than asserting it.\n\n Non-vacuity is the point of the whole test: if
      the sum form and the composed form agreed\n everywhere, the distinction would
      be pedantry. It asserts they disagree by MORE than the\n measurement's own
      noise floor somewhere in the sweep."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
