    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F NEVER 2*acos(|dot|) FOR A POSE METRIC. Up to 0.09 DEGREES
      between BIT-IDENTICAL float32\n quaternions, because acos has infinite derivative
      at 1 and loses half the mantissa there.\n\n This is asserted by MEASUREMENT,
      not by citation: it builds a rotation the way the stream\n composition does
      (five chained products, which Unity does not renormalise), takes its exact\n
      normalisation -- the SAME rotation -- and shows the acos form reports a large
      angle between\n them while the atan2 form the capture uses reports zero.\n\n
      The acos control MUST exceed its floor, or the claim is not being tested at
      all."
    Remarks: 
