  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: Capture_IsHonestOnDegenerateInputs
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A degenerate rig must produce a HONEST row, not a plausible one. Every
      guard in the capture is\n written reject-unless-good -- `!(x > eps)` and never
      `x < eps` -- because NaN fails every\n ordered comparison, so a \"reject if
      bad\" test waves it straight through into a column.\n\n The contract asserted
      here is not \"nothing is ever NaN\": an input carrying NaN SHOULD produce\n
      NonFinite = 1, because saying otherwise would be the capture lying. The contract
      is that\n NonFinite is ACCURATE, and that ordinary degeneracy (coincident joints,
      zero quaternions, no up\n vector) produces finite numbers rather than poison."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
