    Summary: "A STRAIGHT arm along `armDir`, controller rolled `rollDeg` about the
      arm axis away from\n the rig's own anatomical neutral. `bakeBind` false leaves
      the two bind rotations at their struct\n default, which declines the forearm-roll
      stage entirely -- the control.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F ANTI-TAUTOLOGY: the target
      rotation is built from the BIND bone axis and the shoulder->target\n ray. No
      animated bone appears in it, so the sweep cannot be secretly following the
      animation.\n The animated forearm carries a deliberate 25 deg of arbitrary
      clip twist for the same reason."
