  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheStreamReplay_ReproducesTheSolver
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - MakeRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE RUNTIME'S OWN COMPOSITION, REPLAYED. BasisFullBodyIK.SolveTwoBoneIKArms
      ends with\n\n   mid.SetRotation (MidDelta * mid);   root.SetRotation(RootDelta
      * root);\n   root.SetRotation(HintDelta * root); mid.SetRotation(MidPostRoll
      * mid); tip.SetRotation(...)\n\n and setting a PARENT's rotation in an AnimationStream
      carries its children RIGIDLY -- the child's\n world rotation is left-multiplied
      and its position pivots about the parent's origin. Junction\n twists are then
      read from those composed world rotations, never from the result struct's own\n
      bookkeeping, because the bookkeeping is exactly what hid the humeral guard's
      205 mm hand throw."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
