    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheSeamCap_MovesNoJoint_AndDoesNotRelocateTheJump
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - MakeRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The stage is a pure roll about the forearm's own long axis through
      the elbow: the elbow pivots on\n that axis and the hand LIES on it, so neither
      may move -- and the humerus is upstream of the\n stage entirely, so it may
      not jump either.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F THE HUMERUS HALF IS THE \"DID NOT RELOCATE
      IT\" GATE, and it is the one that matters. This\n repo's documented failure
      mode is a clamp that merely moves the kink somewhere else. If a future\n change
      pays for the forearm's continuity by making the humerus jump instead, test
      1 still passes\n and this one fails.\n\n Measured THROUGH THE STREAM, per position
      and per rotation -- not by comparing result-struct\n fields, which is how a
      guard once reported 0.000 mm while throwing the hand 205 mm."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
