  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheTwistBones_DoNotInheritTheSeam
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F THE FOREARM FIX ALONE MOVED THE JUMP INTO THE UPPER ARM.
      THIS IS THE GATE THAT CAUGHT IT.\n\n BasisFullBodyIK.SolveArmTwist hands the
      twist bones a FRACTION of a child's local twist, and a\n fractional map of
      a circle onto itself is discontinuous at +/-180 for every fraction strictly\n
      between 0 and 1: theta = +180 and theta = -180 are the same child, and f*theta
      sends them 360f\n apart. The forearm seam cap in BasisArmSolveCore necessarily
      drives the forearm to 180 deg\n relative to the humerus at the seam -- that
      is what makes the FOREARM continuous -- so it hands\n this stage exactly the
      input that breaks it.\n\n MEASURED with the forearm fixed and this stage NOT
      fixed: the upper-arm twist bone jumped\n 54.10 deg in a single 0.25 deg step,
      which is exactly 360 * 0.15. The arm chain would have\n traded a 160 deg break
      at the elbow for a 54 deg break in the middle of the upper arm.\n\n The fractions
      are the live rig's: BasisFullBodyIK defaults lowerArmTwistFraction 0.5 and\n
      upperArmTwistFraction 0.3, times a twist bone at the segment midpoint (SegmentPositionFraction\n
      0.5), so f = 0.25 and 0.15."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
