  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisArmHintAuthorityTests
    MemberName: BasisArmHintAuthorityTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "DOES THE SOLVER ACTUALLY OBEY THE ELBOW HINT? -- at every extension,
      not just the comfortable ones.\n\n ================================================================================================\n
      THE BUG THIS EXISTS TO PIN, in the user's own words: \"a lot of the time the
      elbow is on the wrong\n side; sometimes it's perfect, then I assign trackers
      again and it's on the wrong side.\"\n\n BasisArmSolveCore faded the hint out
      on `abProj` -- the ELBOW'S OWN LEVER ARM, which collapses to zero\n as the
      arm STRAIGHTENS:\n\n     bendNorm  = abProj.magnitude / totalLen\n     hintFade
      *= Clamp01((bendNorm - 0.0316) / (0.12 - 0.0316))\n\n So past ~97% extension
      the commanded pole was progressively ignored, and past ~99.8% it was ignored\n
      ENTIRELY -- leaving the elbow wherever the base animation put it. The swivel
      model could be perfect and\n never reach the bone.\n\n AND THAT IS WHY IT TRACKED
      CALIBRATION. Give the avatar arms shorter than the user's and their hand\n
      sits at full reach on nearly every frame, so the fade is pinned near zero and
      the model never drives\n the elbow at all. Re-assign trackers, the arm scale
      changes, and the elbow flips sides. \"Sometimes it's\n perfect\" was simply
      the calibrations where the arm happened to stay bent.\n\n The whole POINT of
      predicting a swivel ANGLE is that the hint lands ON the elbow's circle, so
      it stays\n meaningful at every extension and there is nothing to fade. The
      solver was fading it anyway.\n BasisLegSolveCore had already worked this out
      and deleted its copy; the arm's survived.\n ================================================================================================"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
