  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ARealTracker_GetsFullAuthority_AtEveryExtension
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 A REAL ELBOW TRACKER GETS FULL AUTHORITY TOO -- and getting
      this wrong is what has been inverting\n the elbow for anyone who actually straps
      a tracker on.\n\n I first fixed the fade for the MODEL path only and deliberately
      LEFT THE TRACKER'S IN PLACE,\n reasoning that a tracker hint is \"measured,
      a few centimetres off the bone, so it has noise to\n amplify\". That reasoning
      was wrong, and BasisLegSolveCore had already said so in as many words:\n \"the
      POLE is commanded, BY A TRACKER OR BY BendNormal, and it stays perfectly well-defined
      at every\n extension.\"\n\n The fade was never keyed on the tracker's noise.
      It was keyed on abProj -- the CURRENT ELBOW's lever\n arm -- which collapses
      as the arm straightens and has nothing whatsoever to do with the tracker. So\n
      the authority the solver actually granted a real tracker was:\n\n      94%
      extension -> 1.00     98.5% -> 0.62     99.5% -> 0.21     99.9% -> 0.00\n\n
      and 57% of the corpus sits above 95% extension. On most frames of most sessions
      the user's real\n elbow was being blended toward an idle animation they were
      not performing."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
