    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 AND THE SOLVER MUST NOT OVERRULE THE TRACKER WITH A GUESS.\n\n
      The pole-collapse stabilizer eases the elbow toward WORLD-DOWN. It was written
      for the old invented\n lookup pole, which genuinely could point backward along
      the arm and flip. A TRACKER is the user's\n actual elbow -- and because the
      stabilizer engages on |ahProj|, which collapses as the arm\n straightens, it
      engaged HARDEST exactly where the user spends most of their time.\n\n Here
      the tracker says \"elbow out to the side, level\", which is a perfectly ordinary
      human pose. The\n solver must not drag it downward."
