  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheHumeralTwistGuard_DoesNotMoveTheHand_ThroughTheAnimationStream
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - DefaultRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE GUARD MUST NOT MOVE THE HAND -- AND THIS IS THE MEASUREMENT
      THAT CAN SAY SO.\n\n The correction is folded into HintDelta, which the runtime
      applies to the ROOT, which carries\n the forearm and the hand rigidly. Its
      axis is shoulder->ELBOW, and the hand is not on it, so a\n 40 degree correction
      at 90 degrees of elbow flexion orbits the hand 205 mm.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F THE
      ORDER OF THE ASSERTIONS IS THE POINT. The replay is checked against the solver
      on the\n UNGUARDED path FIRST. If those disagree, the replay is wrong and every
      number after it is\n worthless -- and asserting the hand is still with an unfaithful
      replay is precisely the failure\n this test exists to replace."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
