  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: StreamCompose
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 8
    ParamNames:
    - i
    - r
    - elbow
    - hand
    - rootRot
    - midRot
    - false
    - false
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE RUNTIME'S OWN COMPOSITION, REPLAYED IN FULL -- positions
      AND rotations.\n BasisFullBodyIK.SolveTwoBoneIKArms ends with\n     mid.SetRotation(MidDelta*mid);
      root.SetRotation(RootDelta*root);\n     root.SetRotation(HintDelta*root); mid.SetRotation(MidPostRoll*mid);
      tip.SetRotation(TipRotation)\n and setting a PARENT's rotation carries its
      children rigidly: the child's world rotation is\n left-multiplied and its position
      pivots about the parent's origin. HintDelta goes on the ROOT.\n This function
      is the difference between what the solver BOOKKEEPS and what the arm actually
      does.\n\n `skipHint` / `skipPostRoll` exist ONLY so a test can prove this replay
      is SENSITIVE to the stages\n it composes. A replay that agrees with the solver
      because every delta happened to be identity is\n the vacuous-assertion class
      all over again."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
