  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: PoseChangeDeg
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - from
    - c
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F NORMALISE FIRST, AND USE atan2 RATHER THAN acos. Both
      halves matter, and getting either wrong\n puts a 0.1 DEGREE noise floor under
      every measurement in this file.\n\n Chained quaternion products in float32
      drift off the unit sphere by ~1e-6 (Unity does not\n renormalise on multiply,
      and the stream composition chains five of them). The obvious metric,\n 2*acos(|dot|),
      then reports\n\n     acos(1 - 1e-6) = 1.41e-3 rad = 0.081 DEGREES\n\n between
      two quaternions that are BIT-FOR-BIT THE SAME ROTATION -- because acos has
      infinite\n derivative at 1. That is enough to fail an exact reconciliation,
      to fail a rig-convention\n equivariance check, and to inflate the noise floor
      of every continuity sweep here by more than\n the smooth motion those sweeps
      are trying to measure. atan2(|xyz|, |w|) of the RELATIVE rotation\n is well-conditioned
      at zero and costs nothing."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
