  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: GateSmooth
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - ch
    - absFloor
    - amp
    - context
    - 0
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE CONTINUITY GATE, AND WHY IT IS SELF-NORMALISING.\n\n A seam
      is invisible in any single pose and exists only BETWEEN two of them, so the
      measurement is\n always \"worst single-step change over a fine sweep\". The
      hard part is the THRESHOLD: an absolute\n one has to be re-chosen for every
      sweep, every step size and every output unit, and a bad choice\n is how a 1430x
      amplifier ships behind a green suite.\n\n So the scale comes from the sweep
      itself -- the 95th percentile step, which is what this output\n NORMALLY does
      under this input. A smooth sweep has worst ~ p95; a seam has worst >> p95,
      and one\n or two spikes in a thousand samples cannot move p95. The absolute
      floor only says \"below this we\n do not care\", so a sweep whose output barely
      moves cannot fail on noise.\n\n NON-VACUITY IS BUILT IN: p95 == 0 means the
      sweep never moved this output at all, and that is a\n FAILURE, not a pass.
      Returns null when the channel is clean, else the finding."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: KnownOpen
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - defect
    - measured
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 AN INVARIANT THAT IS TRUE, IS ASSERTED, AND IS CURRENTLY BROKEN
      BY SHIPPING CODE.\n\n The alternative to this is one of two bad things: delete
      the assertion, or move the threshold\n until it passes. Both are how a defect
      stops being visible, and moving a threshold is worse\n because it leaves behind
      a test that LOOKS like it is guarding something.\n\n So the invariant stays
      exactly as written, the measured breach is reported in full, and the\n result
      is IGNORED rather than FAILED -- which keeps the suite's failure count meaningful
      while\n putting the number in front of whoever runs it, every single run. When
      the defect is fixed the\n call simply stops being reached and the test goes
      green on its own."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
