    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Runs one parameter sweep and gates every channel. Findings are aggregated
      rather than thrown, so\n a single run names EVERY broken invariant instead
      of dying on the first.\n\n \u2B50 `known*` IS A NAMED, MEASURED ALLOWANCE FOR
      A DEFECT THAT IS ALREADY OPEN -- NOT A TUNING KNOB.\n Two seams are live in
      the shipping core today (see\n BasisArmInvariantNetKnownOpenDefectTests, which
      reproduces each in isolation and\n derives its magnitude in closed form). A
      sweep that reaches one of them would otherwise fail\n forever and drown out
      anything NEW, so the sweep instead carries the defect's own measured size,\n
      NAMED, and stays strict about everything else. The allowance is a CEILING:
      if the known defect\n gets worse, or a second one appears alongside it, the
      sweep still goes red."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
