    Summary: "\u2B50 REACH THROUGH 1.0, WHICH IS WHERE THIS SOLVER LIVES AND WHERE
      ITS GEOMETRY DIES.\n\n 57% of the motion corpus sits above 95% extension, and
      a user whose real arms are longer than\n their avatar's is past full reach
      on EVERY frame. Two things happen in this sweep and nowhere\n else: TriangleAngle
      saturates at 180 and the elbow clamp at MaxElbowAngleDeg takes over (a\n derivative
      change, which must not be a value change), and the elbow's lever arm rho collapses,\n
      which is the ill-conditioning every roll singularity in this file descends
      from."
