    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE HUMERAL TWIST SEAM, SWEPT IN ISOLATION AND HELD TO THE STRICT
      BOUND.\n\n This is the direct regression gate for today's headline fix, measured
      through the STREAM rather\n than off the result struct -- and it is deliberately
      arranged so that NEITHER known-open seam can\n reach it, which is what lets
      it stay strict while the broader sweeps carry allowances:\n\n   * the hand
      points 80 deg DOWN, so the elbow circle is nearly horizontal and its highest
      point\n     sits far below the anatomical ceiling -- BasisElbowAnatomyCore
      is inert for the whole sweep,\n     so D1's side flip cannot occur. The sweep
      ASSERTS that inertness rather than assuming it;\n   * HintRotation is declined,
      so the tracker forearm roll stands down and D2 cannot occur.\n\n What is left
      acting is the swivel and the humeral twist guard, and the guard's seam cap
      is the\n only thing between a smooth tracker orbit and an 80 degree snap of
      the upper arm."
    Remarks: 
