  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: SolvedForearm_DoesNotInheritTheAnimatedForearmRoll
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisArmNet.DefaultRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE ANIMATED FOREARM ROLLS THROUGH A FULL TURN AND THE USER DOES NOT
      MOVE.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F THIS ONE IS NOT A CONTINUITY SWEEP, AND THAT IS THE
      POINT. The correct answer here is that\n the solved arm does not move AT ALL,
      so running it through the continuity runner would trip the\n runner's own \"nothing
      moved, so this sweep is vacuous\" check -- which is right for every OTHER\n
      input and wrong for this one. The property is INVARIANCE, not smoothness: a
      pose the user is\n holding still must not depend on an animation they are not
      performing. Before the no-tracker\n forearm roll landed, the solved forearm
      tracked this 1:1 to 0.000 deg, so the avatar's pronation\n depended on which
      idle clip happened to be playing.\n\n The control is the same sweep with BindLowerArmRotation
      declined -- the pre-fix behaviour, which\n still inherits the animation completely
      -- so the bound carries its own proof that it can fail."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
