    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE POLE'S STAND-OFF FROM THE ARM AXIS, SWEPT FROM HEALTHY TO
      ZERO. This is the axis the old\n BOOLEAN pole gate cliffed on: `ahProj.sqrMagnitude
      > totalLen^2 * 0.001` is |ahProj| > 1.9 cm on\n a 0.6 m arm, and below it the
      hint was not faded but DROPPED, in a single frame, leaving the\n elbow wherever
      the animation had left it. Measured then: the elbow travelled 2582x the hand's
      own\n distance in one step as it crossed. Geometry alone gets you to about
      12x near full extension --\n hundreds is a pole being switched off between
      two frames.\n\n It is also the axis the tracker's own conditioning (TrackerPoleAnchorFrac
      0.03 ->\n TrackerPoleTrustFrac 0.12) is a smoothstep along, and the axis on
      which the anchor hands over\n between refreshing, easing and holding. Three
      separate handovers, one sweep."
