    Summary: "The live rig passes a FINITE HintMaxStepDeg; the offline sweeps pass
      MaxValue. A rate limiter is\n a clamp, and a clamp on a stateless per-frame
      quantity engages and disengages as the input\n crosses it -- which is a gate
      crossing, i.e. the shape of every seam in this file. The budget is\n also SHARED
      between the hint swivel and the pole-collapse stabiliser (one DOF, one budget),
      so\n the point where the hint exhausts it is a second crossing."
