  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisArmInvariantNetHygieneTests
    MemberName: BasisArmInvariantNetHygieneTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: " <summary>\n DETERMINISM, DEGENERACY, AND THE TWO CLASSES THAT ONLY
      SHOW UP OVER TIME.\n\n ================================================================================================\n  
      * DETERMINISM / STATELESSNESS -- the solve is a pure function of its inputs.
      Anything else means\n     the same user pose renders differently depending
      on what happened before it, which is exactly\n     the complaint the no-tracker
      forearm roll was written to answer (the avatar's pronation\n     depended on
      which idle clip was playing).\n\n   * NaN / DEGENERATE HYGIENE -- zero-length
      segments, zero quaternions, collinear arms, a hand\n     exactly at the shoulder,
      a hand past reach. A NaN transform PERSISTS in Unity: the arm never\n     recovers,
      even once good data returns. So nothing may emit NaN and nothing may emit a
      non-unit\n     quaternion, whatever it is handed. The house idiom is \"reject
      unless good\" -- !(x > eps), never\n     x < eps -- because NaN fails every
      ordered comparison and sails straight through the second form.\n\n   * A STALE
      OR DEGENERATE SEED (class 7). MEASURED, 12 noise seeds: a tracker re-acquired
      while the\n     arm was straight seeded its pole from a noise-length vector
      -- a uniformly random direction --\n     and HELD it. The elbow ended 1.9 to
      97.4 degrees off the tracker's actual pole (median ~60) AND\n     STAYED THERE.
      That is a temporal defect: every single frame of it is a perfectly good solve,
      so\n     no per-frame test of any kind can see it. It needs the loop.\n\n  
      * A STRUCTURALLY-ZERO BUDGET (class 6). A gain cap computed its budget from
      AXIS ROTATION alone,\n     so a straight-line reach -- which rotates the axis
      by exactly zero -- froze the joint. The\n     property that catches the class
      is \"a motion that requires no axis rotation must still\n     articulate the
      joint\", and the non-vacuity control is the geometry itself: the triangle solve\n    
      REQUIRES the elbow to travel a known distance as the arm extends.\n ================================================================================================\n
      </summary>"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ArmSolve_IsDeterministic_AndStateless
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Is.GreaterThan(50)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
