    Summary: "Identical inputs must give BIT-IDENTICAL outputs, and the answer must
      not depend on what was\n solved before it. Bit-identical rather than \"close\":
      a solve that is merely close is carrying\n state, and state in a per-frame
      solve is a source of drift that no single-frame gate can see."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
