  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: DegenerateInputs_EmitNoNaN_AndOnlyValidRotations
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisArmNet.DefaultRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Every degeneracy the rig can actually hand this solver, run through
      it. NOTHING may come out as\n NaN or as a non-unit quaternion -- MidPostRoll
      especially, because the runtime multiplies it into\n the forearm UNCONDITIONALLY,
      so the zero quaternion that `default` would leave there is not a\n no-op, it
      collapses the bone.\n\n Deliberately finite-but-degenerate rather than NaN-valued
      positions: the core's reject-unless-good\n guards are written to survive ZERO-LENGTH
      and COLLINEAR geometry, which is what a rig with an\n unbaked bone, a T-posed
      straight arm or a tracker sitting exactly on the arm axis produces."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
