  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: HumerusAndForearm_AxialRoll_StayInsideTheHumanEnvelope
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - StringBuilder(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The two links that ARE bounded, held to their bounds -- with the unguarded
      control on the same\n sweep, so a pass is the guard working and not the sweep
      having gone quiet.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F THE HUMERAL BOUND RELAXES IN THE LAST ~15
      DEG BEFORE THE SEAM AND THAT IS TOPOLOGY, NOT\n SLACK. The twist is a principal
      angle, so any guard maps a CIRCLE onto an ARC; a map that is the\n identity
      inside the arc must either be discontinuous (measured: an 80.009 deg pose jump
      for a\n 0.05 deg input step) or drive the humerus to ZERO twist at 180, which
      is 180 deg from the pose\n being guarded. The guard takes the third option
      -- cap the correction by the distance to the\n seam -- and the price is that
      the hard bound is not enforced in the last 15 deg. Stated here\n rather than
      hidden in a tolerance."
    Remarks: 
