  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: WristAxialRoll_StaysInsideTheHumanEnvelope
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - true
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE HAND'S WORLD ROTATION IS WRITTEN STRAIGHT FROM THE CONTROLLER:
      the solver ends with\n `r.TipRotation = TargetRotation * TargetOffset` and
      the runtime does `tip.SetRotation(TipRotation)`.\n So every degree of controller
      roll that the forearm and the humerus do not absorb lands in the\n WRIST JOINT
      -- a joint that has no axial degree of freedom at all. This is the SAME SHAPE
      as the\n humeral defect that shipped: a DOF driven 1:1 from a tracker with
      nothing bounding it, sitting\n next to several carefully-bounded neighbours.\n\n
      The relief and the forearm roll are the absorbers, and they are bounded (70
      deg of relief, an\n 80 deg comfort band), so what is left over past those is
      structurally unbounded.\n\n This test states the ANATOMICAL invariant. If it
      is red, that is a FINDING and the number in the\n message is the finding --
      do not relax the constant to make it green."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
