  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisArmReachBehindTests
    MemberName: BasisArmReachBehindTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"When we reach behind with our arms there is snapping.\"\n\n ================================================================================================\n
      WHAT THE SNAP WAS, AND WHY THESE TESTS SWEEP AZIMUTH.\n\n The no-tracker elbow
      bend is a UNIT TANGENT field on the sphere of hand directions, so by\n Poincare-Hopf
      it must carry zeros of total index 2. BasisElbowFieldModel (a global polynomial)\n
      split that into two index-1 zeros, and one of them sat in REACHABLE workspace:
      down-and-back,\n azimuth ~130 deg, ~20 deg below level -- hand out behind the
      hip, arm bent. Reaching behind.\n\n BasisArmBigSwingFlipTests already sweeps
      MERIDIANS (up-down swings) and permits a hard rotation\n only inside a collapsed-lever
      core. But the reach-behind core is crossed on a HORIZONTAL path --\n swinging
      the hand around from the front to behind you -- which no meridian sweep touches.
      That is\n the coverage gap these tests close: constant-elevation AZIMUTH sweeps,
      front to behind.\n\n The fix (BasisElbowStereoModel, default via BasisElbowFieldModel.UseStereoField)
      carries a SINGLE\n index-2 zero and places it straight across the body, inside
      the torso, where no hand can point.\n The entire reachable workspace is then
      zero-free. These tests pin both halves: the snap is gone in\n reach, AND the
      one unavoidable zero is unreachable. Measured on 199,528 real frames the reach-behind\n
      worst step fell 33 deg/frame -> 0.3, and the worst reachable elbow gain ~106x
      -> 7x.\n ================================================================================================"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ReachingBehind_DoesNotSnapTheElbow_OnAnyHorizontalSwing
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50\u2B50 THE COMPLAINT, GATED. Swing the hand from straight ahead
      around to behind you at a fixed\n height, in fine steps, and measure how far
      the bend rotates per step. This is the exact path\n the user traverses reaching
      behind, and it is the one BasisArmBigSwingFlipTests' meridians miss.\n\n On
      BasisElbowFieldModel this sweep rotated the hint 33 degrees in a single 0.25-degree
      hand step\n at reach 0.65, elevation -20 (hand behind the hip). Here it must
      stay smooth at every height,\n because the stereo field has no zero anywhere
      the hand can reach. Gate 8 deg; measured worst ~0.7."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
