    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheReachableWorkspace_HasNoBendCollapse_TheOneZeroIsInTheTorso
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50\u2B50 THE TOPOLOGY, PINNED. A tangent field must have a zero
      (index total 2); the whole point of\n the stereo model is that its ONE zero
      lives in the torso. So sweep the entire sphere and demand\n the bend's conditioning
      (its lever) never collapses ANYWHERE the hand can actually go. The only\n place
      it is allowed to fall is deep across the body -- x well negative -- where a
      hand would have\n to pass through the chest to point, which is unreachable
      at every reach.\n\n If a future re-fit (or a different zero placement) let
      a collapse back into reachable space, this\n fails -- which is precisely the
      regression that reintroduces the snap."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
