  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: Recorder_FiringRateDenominatorIsAvailability_SoADeadGuardCannotReadAsAQuietOne
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 \"0.0%\" AND \"n/a\" MEAN OPPOSITE THINGS, AND THE DIFFERENCE
      IS A SHIPPED DEFECT.\n\n A guard that fires 0 times out of 22032 frames it
      COULD have fired in is a tuned guard doing\n nothing, which is a defect. A
      guard that fires 0 times out of 0 frames it could have fired in\n is a guard
      that was never wired up, which is a different defect with a different fix.
      Divide by\n total frames and the second one prints as the reassuring first
      one.\n\n So the denominator is availability. This feeds a session in which
      the twist guard is never\n available and asserts the report says so, then feeds
      one in which it is available and quiet and\n asserts THAT prints as a rate
      -- because if both printed \"n/a\" the distinction would be lost the\n other
      way round."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
