  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheAppliedRoll_StaysOnItsPrincipalBranch_AndInsideTheSeamEnvelope
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisArmNet.DefaultRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 `roll` IS A SUM OF TWO PRINCIPAL ANGLES AND SO IS NOT ONE, AND
      PAST 180 THE BOUND VANISHED.\n\n seam = PI - |roll| goes NEGATIVE there, so
      `pull` is rejected by the reject-unless-good test and\n the saturation is skipped
      along with it: the stage applied the raw demand, unbounded. Measured\n pre-wrap
      demands of 214.9 deg on the sweep above, i.e. a 214.9 deg forearm roll out
      of a stage\n whose stated hard bound is 120.\n\n The gate is the applied roll's
      own magnitude, read through the stream, against the ONLY bound the\n fix claims:
      the eased-out envelope can reach 180 and no further, because +180 and -180
      are the\n same rotation and that is where the correction goes to zero."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
