  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: BelowTheCrossing_TheAppliedRollIsTheUnchangedSaturation
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - stale."
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 BELOW THE CROSSING THE FIX IS THE EXACT IDENTITY WITH THE OLD
      SATURATION, AND THIS PROVES IT\n WITHOUT THE OLD CODE. `pull = mag - Saturate(mag)`
      and `seam = 180 - mag` cross at 144.686 deg\n (derived here from the two constants,
      not written down), and below that the min() does not bind.\n So every ordinary
      pronation is bit for bit what it was -- which is what makes this a seam fix\n
      rather than a re-tune of the forearm."
    Remarks: 
