  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheTrackerSeamCap_MovesNoJoint_AndDoesNotRelocateTheJump
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F THIS REPO'S DOCUMENTED FAILURE MODE IS A CLAMP THAT MOVES
      THE KINK SOMEWHERE ELSE. The\n no-tracker sibling's fix did exactly that once:
      capping the forearm alone drove the forearm to\n 180 deg relative to the humerus
      at the seam, which is precisely the input a FRACTIONAL twist map\n is discontinuous
      on, and the upper-arm twist bone then jumped 54.10 deg (= 360 * 0.15).\n\n
      The tracker cap drives the forearm to the SAME 180 deg at the SAME seam, so
      it hands\n BasisTwistSolveCore the same input. Everything downstream of the
      forearm is therefore measured\n here, through the stream, over the same sweep:\n\n  
      * the ELBOW and the HAND -- a roll about the forearm's own long axis pivots
      on the elbow and\n     the hand LIES on that axis, so neither may move at all;\n  
      * the HUMERUS -- entirely upstream of the stage, so it may not jump;\n   *
      the WRIST junction -- the hand is written verbatim from the controller, so
      whatever the\n     forearm does not absorb lands there;\n   * both TWIST BONES,
      driven exactly as BasisFullBodyIK.SolveArmTwist drives them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheStage_DeclinesExactlyWhenTheTrackerSendsNoRotation
    Kind: Method
