    Summary: "A GLITCH IS NOT NOISE. A lighthouse puck occasionally jumps a centimetre
      or two -- occlusion, an IMU\n pop, a reflection. The solve is stateless and
      unclamped (HintMaxStepDeg = MaxValue from the live\n job), so nothing between
      the puck and the bone can absorb that: whatever the glitch commands, the\n
      elbow does, that frame.\n\n This does not assert the glitch is filtered --
      it is not, and pretending otherwise would be a test\n that passes while proving
      nothing. It asserts the two things that must survive one anyway: the hand\n
      stays exactly on target, and the elbow stays inside the anatomical envelope."
    Remarks: 
