    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: " <summary>\n \u2B50 A MIS-STRAPPED TRACKER CANNOT PUT THE ELBOW ABOVE
      THE SHOULDER.\n\n The tracker path skips the pole-collapse stabilizer entirely
      (`if (HintWeight && !HintIsTracker)`),\n takes no fade, takes no rate limit
      and takes no One-Euro. So a tracker mounted upside down, rotated\n round the
      arm, or simply strapped to the wrong limb has NOTHING standing between it and
      the bone --\n except BasisElbowAnatomyCore, which runs last and guards the
      OUTCOME.\n\n So it must hold here. Command the elbow STRAIGHT UP (the chicken
      wing the user reported) from a\n tracker, and the elbow must still come to
      rest at or below the higher of shoulder and hand.\n </summary>"
    Remarks: 
