    Summary: "Even arm-twist distribution. A single twist bone (forearm / upper-arm)
      must absorb a share of the bone's\n roll equal to its POSITION along the bone,
      so the roll spreads as a linear gradient instead of piling up\n at one joint
      -- the \"candy-wrapper\" the user sees as the arm \"fully twisting at points\".
      Exercises\n BasisTwistSolveCore.SegmentPositionFraction + BasisTwistSolveCore.Solve,
      the\n same path `BasisFullIKConstraintJob.SolveArmTwist` runs live (it sets
      Fraction = positionFraction *\n distributionStrength)."
