  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheCorrection_IsAPureRollAboutTheSolvedForearm
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - true
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE CORRECTION IS A PURE ROLL ABOUT THE SOLVED FOREARM'S OWN LONG AXIS
      -- the one axis on which\n it can bound the wrist without changing where the
      hand points relative to the arm.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F NOTE WHAT IS DELIBERATELY
      *NOT* ASSERTED HERE, because asserting it would be the vacuous-gate\n class
      again: \"the hand does not move\". TipRotation carries no position and the
      stream never reads\n it when placing a joint, so a hand-position check here
      would compare two numbers this stage\n cannot affect and would pass no matter
      what axis the correction used. The falsifiable statement\n is the AXIS, and
      it is the one that dies if the correction is ever applied about shoulder->hand\n
      or about the target direction instead."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
