  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheBound_IsContinuous_ThroughAFullTurnOfTheController
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisArmNet.DefaultRig(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 A FULL TURN OF THE CONTROLLER, IN 0.02 DEG STEPS, THROUGH THE
      +/-180 SEAM.\n\n Every principal-angle clamp in this file has had this defect
      and three of them shipped with it:\n a bare min/max onto an arc sends two hand
      poses 0.02 deg apart to two hands 2*bound apart.\n Measured amplifications
      when they were live: 1430x (humeral guard) and 3201x (no-tracker forearm).\n\n
      The wrist bound caps the BOUND by the distance to the seam rather than the
      PULL, which is the\n opposite of what its three siblings do -- capping the
      pull would leave the wrist AT 180 deg,\n which is the entire defect. It can
      afford to, and that is the whole reason this stage is the easy\n one: 15 deg
      has 165 deg of room to reach the seam in, so the return slope is 15/165 = 0.09."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
