    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE MEASUREMENT THAT CHOSE THE RESIDUAL POLICY, PINNED SO \"JUST
      RECRUIT MORE FOREARM\" IS\n REFUTED BY A NUMBER RATHER THAN RE-ARGUED EVERY
      TIME SOMEONE READS THIS FILE.\n\n The alternative to dropping is to make the
      forearm and the humerus absorb more before the wrist\n has to. That is only
      possible if they have room WHEN THE WRIST BREACHES, and they do not. The\n
      forearm's ceiling here is the researched flexion-dependent, sign-asymmetric
      one --\n sup_max = clamp(50 + 0.35*flex, 50, 85), pro_max = clamp(85 - 0.20*flex,
      55, 85), which collapses\n toward 50 at a straight arm because the biceps cannot
      supinate with the elbow extended -- and the\n LOOSER of the two signs is used,
      so this is the most generous reading available."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
