    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "WHAT DROPPING COSTS, IN THE UNITS A VIEWER ACTUALLY PERCEIVES. The
      correction is a pure roll about\n the forearm, so the hand's POSITION is untouched
      and its POINTING direction moves only as far as\n that roll carries it. What
      the user loses is palm ROLL.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F THE TRACKER PATH IS REPORTED
      TWICE ON PURPOSE. The envelope sweep rolls the elbow tracker and\n the controller
      INDEPENDENTLY, which manufactures poses no strapped puck can produce -- a forearm\n
      measured at +101.8 deg under a hand measured at -75.5. The bound has to survive
      those, so they are\n swept. But the cost a real user pays is the CORRELATED
      one, where the puck is on the arm holding\n the controller, and quoting only
      the decorrelated figure would overstate it by 4x."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
