  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ElbowStrapClockAngle_DoesNotReachTheForearm
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - off
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "An elbow tracker is rigid on the forearm: trackerRot(t) = foreRot(t)
      * K, with K the strap offset.\n K's clock angle around the limb is ARBITRARY
      and carries no pronation information, so it must not\n reach the forearm. Calibration
      stores Qref = Inverse(trackerWorld) * boneWorld = Inverse(K), and the\n rig
      driver feeds trackerRot_live * Qref, which recovers the true forearm for any
      K.\n\n Measured before the mapping was added: a 90 deg strap angle produced
      80.6 deg of forearm roll at zero\n pronation, swinging the wrist residual from
      +26.4 to -54.2 deg. LowerArm has no Recalibrated* offset,\n so nothing else
      in the pipeline was cancelling it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
