  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisCalibrationHeightTests
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationHeightTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Regression tests for the calibration \"feel\" math (BasisCalibrationMath.ComputeDeviceScale),\n
      the formula BasisHeightDriver.ChooseHeightToUse runs to turn a measured eye
      height into the\n DeviceScale the camera is scaled by. The avatar feels right
      iff the DeviceScale denominator equals the\n player's TRUE standing eye height;
      these pin what happens when it doesn't -- the cause of the report that\n people
      must nudge once or twice to stop feeling too tall.\n\n Backends measure the
      denominator differently: OpenXR binds the head to centerEyePosition so the
      tracked\n point IS the eye (eyeReference 0), while OpenVR tracks the HMD pose
      origin sitting a gap g below the eyes\n and bridges it with CenterEyeVerticalOffset.
      If that bridge under-reports the gap (or is 0 because the\n SteamVR eye transform
      wasn't ready at capture), the denominator is short and the avatar renders too
      tall."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
