  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisCalibrationOffsetReprojectionTests
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationOffsetReprojectionTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Regression tests for FBT position-offset reprojection\n (BasisCalibrationMath.ReprojectInverseOffsetPosition):
      the mechanism that lets a\n T-pose calibration keep fitting after an avatar
      swap, a scale-slider change, or a device\n reconnect \u2014 WITHOUT redoing
      the T-pose. Rotation calibration has had this since 2026-06 (the\n s_ref mechanism);
      positions were left stale, so every swap/scale change degraded FBT fit until\n
      a manual recalibration.\n\n The reprojection rebuilds the calibration geometry
      from scale-free snapshots (tracker + head in\n unscaled device space) at the
      current DeviceScale/OffsetCoords, anchors the avatar with\n DriveTpose's own
      math, and re-captures the offset against the current avatar's T-pose bind.\n
      These tests pin the exactness properties that make that valid: same-state reprojection
      is a\n no-op, and after any scale / proportion / frame change the bone lands
      exactly on the rebuilt\n reference. All assertions are exact math (small float
      tolerances only)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisCalibrationScaleFreshnessTests
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationScaleFreshnessTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Regression tests for the calibration scale-freshness rule: the tracker
      offset capture\n (BasisCalibrationMath.ComputeInverseOffset, fed by BasisInput.CalculateOffset)
      must\n read tracker coords produced at the SAME DeviceScale as the avatar-bone
      references it captures\n against.\n\n FullBodyCalibration recomputes DeviceScale
      mid-pass (ApplyScaleAndHeight, after the T-pose\n re-captures the avatar eye
      height), but every input's ScaledDeviceCoord was produced by the LAST\n device
      poll \u2014 at the PRE-calibration scale. Capturing offsets from those stale
      coords against\n new-scale references bakes a position error of |s1 - s0| x
      |unscaled pose| into every tracker:\n the \"calibrate two or three times until
      the avatar fits\" convergence, where each pass shrinks the\n scale delta until
      the offsets finally capture clean. The fix re-runs the scale-dependent tail
      of\n the poll (BasisInput.RefreshScaledDeviceCoordFromLastPoll) before anything
      reads the coords;\n these tests pin the arithmetic of both the failure and
      the fix using the runtime's own helpers."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisCalibrationSwapTests
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationSwapTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
