    Summary: "BasisTrackerConfigMatrixTests.BuildRig, mirrored. Per clip the chain
      is rebuilt from THAT\n subject's own segment vectors at their most upright
      frame, so proportions and natural curvature\n are the subject's and not an
      invented stack. Every bone binds at identity rotation, which is why\n the chest
      and pelvis feeds are DELTAS off the subject's own rest frames.\n\n standingHeadHeight
      / crouchDepth are deliberately absent: every row here runs with a hips\n tracker,
      and ApplyCrouchBodyOffset returns immediately when `HasChestTracker || hasHipsTracker`,\n
      so there is no crouch stage on either branch to feed. The pelvis-synthesis
      stages being off is\n the point -- it is what \"hips pinned\" means and what
      makes a chest delta attributable."
