    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE COMPLAINT, DIRECTLY. Chest tracker on, hips pinned, tracker held
      at the frame's own\n measurement, and only the head moves. The chest must not
      follow it.\n\n The second assertion is the ANTI-TAUTOLOGY CONTROL and is not
      optional. It runs the identical\n sweep on the identical rig with HasChestTracker
      flipped false -- the branch that has no term for\n the chest at all -- and
      requires that coupling to be LARGE. A harness whose chest simply never\n moved
      (a dead solve, an unfed target, a chain indexed root->tip so the \"chest\"
      is really the neck)\n would sail through the first assertion and fail this
      one. Both numbers come out of one function,\n on one rig, with one flag between
      them."
    Remarks: 
