    Summary: "SCOPE. ReassertTrackedChest is gated on HasChestTracker, so the 3-point
      / hips-only user must be\n bit-unaffected -- and on that branch a hand->chest
      coupling is not a bug, it is\n ApplyArmSwingChestFollow doing exactly what
      it ships to do (measured 27.07 deg per metre of\n lateral hand swing). If this
      ever collapsed toward zero, the change would have leaked out of the\n tracker
      branch and quietly frozen every desktop user's torso.\n\n The tracked side
      is asserted too, from the other direction: with a chest tracker the arm-swing\n
      follow is skipped by design (that branch owns chest rotation directly) and
      measures 0.02 deg/m,\n so the reassert must not have introduced a new hand
      path into the chest."
