  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisCrouchBindFrameTests
    MemberName: BasisCrouchBindFrameTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bind-frame regression for the crouch sit-back (BasisCrouchOffsetCore).
      As the head\n drops the hips slide BACKWARD along the body's forward so a squat
      reads as sitting back. \"Backward\"\n was `HipsRot * Vector3.forward` -- the
      hips BONE's local +Z, which is a rig convention. On a Blender-\n exported rig
      the hips bind is rolled \u221290 about X, so that +Z is world-UP: the slide
      went vertical and,\n once the vertical component was stripped, collapsed to
      zero and the crouch silently never fired.\n\n The fix cancels the hips bind
      (offsetRotationHips) to get the anatomical forward. These guard that the\n
      slide is the same anatomical backward move for every bind convention, and that
      a degenerate/absent bind\n falls back to the old HipsRot-forward behaviour
      bit for bit (so the sweep and equivariance test, which\n pass identity / default,
      are unchanged)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
