    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards the declared-body-length ceiling, and guards it BY MESSAGE rather
      than merely by \"it\n threw\". This exists because the first version of that
      ceiling was dead code: it compared an\n int32 body length against a long constant
      of 3.89e9 that no int32 can exceed, so it never fired\n and the compiler said
      so (CS0652). A test that only asserted \"some exception\" would have passed\n
      against the dead guard, because an oversized length also trips the truncation
      check further\n down. Asserting the specific message is what makes this test
      able to fail."
    Remarks: 
