  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: RecordedTimestep_SurvivesRoundTripExactly
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisDeviceStreamFlags.DeflateBody)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards the FRAMERATE hazard. This codebase has shipped real framerate-dependent
      blends \u2014 a\n saturate(dt*speed) smoother whose time constant tracked GPU
      speed, and a self-referential slerp\n that converged by frame count rather
      than elapsed time. A replay at a different rate is\n therefore a different
      experiment, so the recorded timestep must survive exactly or a caller\n cannot
      even tell whether its replay rate matched. The corpus contains a deliberate
      41 ms hitch\n at frame 61 for this reason; a codec that resampled to a uniform
      rate would erase it.\n Headroom: none by design (bit comparison)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
