  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: FollowPoseReconstruction_RepublishesRecordedScaledPose
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BuildCorpus(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards the injection seam itself. The replay feeds simulated devices
      by writing a FollowMovement\n local pose; BasisInputXRSimulate.LateDoPollData
      then maps that forward into ScaledDeviceCoord,\n which is what actually reaches
      the bone. This test runs the reconstruction and then the REAL\n forward map
      and requires the recorded scaled pose to come back out \u2014 i.e. that the
      replayed\n device publishes exactly what the headset published. Without this
      the replay could be perfectly\n deterministic and perfectly wrong.\n\n Headroom:
      tolerance 1e-5 m against a measured max of 3.66 um over 400,000 random pose/offset\n
      pairs at these ranges (mean 0.44 um) = 2.7x. Rotation tolerance 1e-6 componentwise
      against a\n measured max of 2.384e-07 (1 ULP at unit magnitude) = 4.2x. Componentwise,
      not Quaternion.Angle:\n acos(dot) is ill-conditioned near identity and reports
      up to 0.105 deg of spurious error on data\n that is exact to 1 ULP."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
