    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: FollowPoseReconstruction_IsImmuneToOffsetCoordsDrift
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 6f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards against OffsetCoords drift. OffsetCoords is a process-global
      that the playspace mover and\n calibration both write, so it will generally
      NOT match the recording at replay time. The\n reconstruction solves against
      the LIVE value precisely so the republished scaled pose is\n unchanged \u2014
      this test proves that immunity by replaying the same stream under a wildly\n
      different offset and requiring the same scaled pose out. If this regressed,
      every replay run\n after a playspace nudge would silently shift the whole body.\n
      Headroom: as above, 2.7x on position / 4.2x on rotation."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
