  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheLateralSeed_PredictsTheSideRealElbowsChoose_WellAboveChance
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - LoadCorpus(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 DOES THE BODY-LATERAL AXIS ACTUALLY PREDICT WHICH SIDE REAL
      ELBOWS SIT ON?\n\n The seed exists to make hysteresis hold an anatomically-outward
      elbow rather than whichever side\n float noise picked on the first frame. That
      is only worth doing if \"outward\" is where real\n elbows go. So: over every
      corpus arm-frame with a well-conditioned side, compare\n sign(dot(lateralOut,
      w)) against the real elbow's own sign(s), and require agreement WELL above\n
      chance.\n\n \u26A0 A COIN FLIP MUST FAIL THIS. If the corpus says real elbows
      are symmetric about the mirror\n plane, the seed is decoration and BasisElbowAnatomyCore
      should stop taking lateralOut at all --\n hysteresis alone is what removes
      the buzz, and it does not need this input. Do not weaken the\n bound to keep
      the seed; delete the seed."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
