    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F THE FIX THAT LOOKS RIGHT AND IS NOT. Deciding the branch
      by the body-lateral axis inside a\n dead band quietens s = 0 and opens an identical
      cut at the band's EDGE. Pinned because this is\n the shape a future revision
      will reach for first, and the reason it is wrong is a measurement,\n not an
      opinion.\n\n The lateral-only shape is reconstructed here rather than shipped:
      the core is asked for its\n geometry through the public overloads, and the
      branch is re-decided outside it."
