  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheCutIsForced_NoContinuousGuardIsBothIdentityOnLegalAndEnforcing
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - StringBuilder(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE TOPOLOGICAL OBSTRUCTION, MACHINE-CHECKED. Discretise the
      circle and ask directly: is\n there ANY assignment of guarded azimuths that
      is the identity on legal inputs, never leaves the\n elbow above the hard limit,
      and never moves more than G times the input's own step?\n\n The answer is no
      for any bounded G, and the minimum feasible G is measured here. It DIVERGES
      as\n the firing arc shrinks, which is the price of the only continuous alternative
      (shape C, the\n traverse) and the reason the shipped guard takes a jump instead.
      This owes nothing to the\n guard's inputs, which is precisely why no new input
      can remove D1's pop."
    Remarks: 
