    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 WHAT THE TIE BAND COSTS ON THE ORIGINAL DEFECT. Hysteresis holds
      the side across the top, so\n a sweep that crosses the cut now flips at the
      band's far edge instead of at the top: the SAME\n number of flips (one), a
      slightly different place, and a jump that grows by the difference\n between
      phiG at the band edge and phiG at the top.\n\n This is the \"what did the residual
      move into\" measurement, stated as a number rather than a\n claim, and bounded
      so a future change cannot quietly make it worse."
    Remarks: 
