  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: AtTheExtensionCap_TheOldRuleFiresNever_AndTheLiveCoreFires
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - 0.5f
    - lower
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE CHECK THAT MAKES THIS FILE MEAN SOMETHING. Both halves run on the
      SAME grid at the SAME\n extension -- BasisArmSolveCore.MaxElbowAngleDeg, where
      the solver actually parks a stretched arm:\n\n   the OLD rule (a flat SoftMarginFracLimb
      of the arm) fires on ZERO of 22,032 poses;\n   the LIVE core fires on a healthy
      fraction of the same 22,032.\n\n The first half is the defect, demonstrated,
      not asserted-absent. A gate that only checked the\n second half would have
      passed just as happily on a guard that was already working, and would\n therefore
      have proved nothing about the change that made it work."
    Remarks: 
