  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheAnatomyGuardAndTheHumeralTwistGuardDoNotFight
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - 0.30f
    - 0.30f
    - 0.0872f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0 THE TWO GUARDS ARE NOT DISJOINT, AND THE COMMENT THAT SAID THEY
      WERE WAS WRONG.\n BasisArmSolveCore's humeral twist guard acts about shoulder->ELBOW;
      this one about\n shoulder->HAND. Those are (180-theta)/2 apart: 45 deg at 90
      deg of flexion -- genuinely\n different degrees of freedom -- but only 5.00
      deg apart at MaxElbowAngleDeg, which is precisely\n where this fix acts. At
      full extension they are very nearly the SAME axis.\n\n What saves the composition
      is ORDER and GEOMETRY, not separation: the anatomy guard runs first\n and sets
      the elbow; the twist guard runs second, re-measures from the corrected elbow,
      and\n rotates about an axis the elbow LIES ON -- so it cannot move the elbow,
      and cannot put it back\n above the ceiling. This test holds that reasoning
      to the actual solver: the achieved envelope\n must be identical with the twist
      guard engaged and declined.\n\n (Measured while writing this: at the offending
      pose the twist guard reads 90.0 deg against its\n 120 deg soft limit and contributes
      0.0 -- it never covered this hole and could not have.)"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: RealHumansAreNotClipped_SegmentedByExtensionBand
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (a.Fired
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Every arm-frame of the corpus, measured through the SHIPPING core in
      the SHIPPING frame -- the\n chest's up, which is the only frame the ceiling
