  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisElbowAnatomyTests
    MemberName: BasisElbowAnatomyTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "AN ELBOW CANNOT POINT AT THE SKY.\n\n The report: \"the arms are able
      to get in rotations that are not possible, I'm still seeing the\n occasional
      arm bending up (so the elbows point to the sky).\"\n\n The KNEE has been hard-guarded
      into its anatomical half-space for a long time (BasisLegSolveCore:\n \"a knee
      behind that axis is not unnatural, it is anatomically unrepresentable\"). THE
      ARM HAD NO SUCH\n GUARD AT ALL -- nothing stopped the solver placing the elbow
      anywhere on its circle, including straight\n up. BasisElbowAnatomyCore closes
      that, and this file is the proof, in both directions:\n\n   * it makes the
      impossible pose UNREACHABLE, and\n   * it leaves every possible pose BYTE FOR
      BYTE untouched.\n\n The second half matters as much as the first. A guard that
      perturbs legal poses to fix illegal ones is\n the wrong trade, and it is how
      guards end up being deleted by the next person."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
