    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50\u2B50 THE FLIP. THIS IS THE TEST THAT WAS MISSING.\n\n A snap
      is invisible in any single pose -- every individual frame looks perfectly reasonable.
      It only\n exists BETWEEN frames. So sweep the hand through the singularity
      in fine steps and measure JOINT\n TRAVEL PER UNIT OF HAND TRAVEL. (The methodology
      is the project's own, from the arm/leg hint-extension\n snap work.)\n\n The
      sweep is the pose that broke the shipped model: hand directly under the shoulder
      with the elbow\n BENT -- arms relaxed at your sides, a hand on your hip, a
      weapon at low-ready. The hand sways fore-aft\n the way a standing human's does
      when they breathe.\n\n MEASURED HERE: shipped model 49 deg / 19.6 cm of elbow
      for 3 cm of hand. This model, same sweep,\n peaks at well under 1x. A real
      elbow tracks its hand at 0.5-1.5x; the gate is 3x, which is far above\n anything
      anatomical and far below anything that reads as a flip."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
