    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The two arms must be exact mirrors. A sign error here is \"one elbow
      is fine and the other is\n inverted\", which is precisely what a user reports
      when the mirror is wrong -- and this project has\n got the mirror wrong twice,
      once by 145 degrees.\n\n The model is evaluated in a frame whose +x is OUTWARD
      for BOTH arms, so mirroring is the identity on\n the model itself: feed it
      the same numbers and it must return the same numbers. That is a stronger\n
      statement than \"the two arms look symmetric\", and it is the one that catches
      a stray negation."
