  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisElbowFullCircleTests
    MemberName: BasisElbowFullCircleTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards the FULL-CIRCLE swivel search in BasisElbowProtectCore.\n\n
      ================================================================================================\n
      WHAT THIS IS FOR. The protect used to sweep only the arc from the natural pole
      to outDir. That is\n a DOMAIN limit, not a resolution limit: measured against
      the live arm solve over 11 759 reachable\n hand targets, 39.1% of the poses
      it gave up on had a clearing elbow sitting on the same circle,\n just outside
      the sampled arc -- 68.4% past outDir and 31.6% on the inward side, which was
      never\n looked at at all. Widening the domain took the cleared fraction from
      0.6708 to 0.7995 at the SAME\n sample count, because the feasible arcs are
      wide (median widest arc 67 deg, only 0.6% narrower\n than the old 7.5 deg spacing).\n\n
      THE DOMAIN AND THE SELECTION RULE ONLY WORK AS A PAIR. Full circle with the
      old \"smallest\n swing wins\" rule is a REGRESSION -- measured over 30 hand
      slides it popped 145 deg in a single\n frame, 25 times, against 54 deg / 4
      times for the shipped one-sided sweep -- because a wider\n domain makes the
      feasible set genuinely disconnected and a stateless argmax hops between\n components
      as they open and close. Anchoring on last frame's answer removes that.\n\n
      BUT THE DOMAIN AND THE ANCHOR ARE INDEPENDENT KNOBS, AND CONFLATING THEM MEASURED
      BACKWARDS.\n They were originally one flag, and because an absent anchor defaults
      to ZERO -- a pull toward the\n natural pole, not a neutral start -- the 354k-point
      sweep read the cleared fraction going the WRONG\n WAY, 0.3606 -> 0.3552, with
      mean swing FALLING 12.68 -> 11.70 deg. FullCircle widens the search;\n HasPrevSwivel
      says an established previous choice exists. Keep them separate.\n\n So there
      are two things worth gating, and they pull in opposite directions: the search
      has to\n find MORE (Clears_StrictlyMorePoses_ThanTheOneSidedSweep) and it has
      to move LESS\n (TheChosenSwivel_DoesNotHop_AsTheHandSlides). A fix that only
      does one of them is the bug.\n ================================================================================================"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
