  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheConditioningGate_IsWhatProtectsTheCore
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50\u2B50 THE CORE, AND THE CONTROL THAT PROVES THIS TEST CAN FAIL.\n\n
      Radial budget must never help a topological core flip. The adversarial trajectory
      is a hand\n CRAWLING through a core (+/-1.5 deg of azimuth over the whole run,
      so rotation budget alone is\n near zero and the old cap is effectively frozen)
      while simultaneously PUNCHING -- 0.30 arm\n lengths of extension over 20 frames.\n\n
      Two assertions, and the second is the one that keeps the first honest:\n  
      1. gated == rotation-only, to the bit. The conditioning gate is identically
      zero at a core, so\n      the fix cannot have changed anything here.\n   2.
      with the gate DEFEATED the same trajectory leaks a double-digit step. Without
      this the\n      first assertion would also pass against a cap that ignored
      dReach entirely."
    Remarks: 
