    Summary: "Guards BasisElbowSwingCapCore -- the stateful half of the reach-behind
      fix. It keeps\n the accurate elbow field (correct out-and-back pose) and bounds
      how fast the bend may rotate\n relative to the HAND, so a topological core
      flips the elbow no faster than a human elbow tracks\n (gain ~1x, p99 4.6x measured)
      instead of teleporting.\n\n These drive the core through the SAME sequence
      the job feeds it: a hand sweeping through\n BasisElbowFieldModel's down-and-back
      core (azimuth ~130, ~20 below level), which is where the raw\n field flips
      ~70 deg in half a degree of hand motion."
    Remarks: 
