    Summary: " <summary>Run a hand trajectory through the cap, returning the capped
      bend per frame.</summary>\n <summary>\n \u2B50\u2B50 THE BOUND. Sweeping the
      hand through the core, the capped bend may never rotate (about the\n current
      shoulder->hand axis) by more than MaxGain times the hand's own rotation that
      frame. That\n is the whole guarantee: the reach-behind flip is bounded to the
      human tracking ceiling. On the\n raw field this same sweep flips ~70 deg in
      one 0.5-degree step (gain ~140x); capped it is <= 5x.\n </summary>"
