    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "BasisLocalFootDriver.InitializeVariables measures the leg segments
      off the authored T-pose, and\n BasisLocalRigDriver.RefreshBodyFit rescales
      those same segments AFTERWARDS (BasisBodyFitApply bones\n 8-11 are the lower
      legs and feet, whose LOCAL POSITIONS are the thigh and shin). Until the driver's\n
      only rescale hook learned about AppliedBodyFit.LegScale it applied ScaledToMatchValue
      alone, so the\n recorded leg length described a body the avatar no longer had.\n\n
      BasisFootSimulateJob derives bendRatio = 1 - saturate(hipFootUpDist / avgLeg)
      and multiplies\n kneeSplay by it, so understating avgLeg narrows the knees.
      MEASURED against the real job at the\n reference avatar (0.87 m leg, 0.18 m
      stance): the loss is 12-31% of the splay, NOT a collapse --\n kneeMinSide floors
      the separation at half stance (9.00 cm) and bendRatio does not fully saturate\n
      at plausible reach/scale pairs. reach 0.78 + legScale 1.30 => 13.29 -> 9.18
      cm (30.9% lost);\n reach 0.82 + legScale 1.20 => 12.57 -> 9.69 cm (23.0%);
      reach 0.95 + legScale 1.20 => 12.0%.\n LegScale is derived per avatar, so the
      error is re-rolled on every swap."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
