    Summary: "At rest, FootRotation must reproduce the foot bone's T-pose world rotation
      EXACTLY.\n\n footAlign is the bone measured in the rest frame: inverse(restFrame)
      * boneRestRot. So at rest, where\n the target frame IS the rest frame, frame
      * footAlign collapses to boneRestRot by construction. This\n holds for ANY
      rig -- the foot bone's axes never enter into it, which is the entire point.
      A rig whose\n foot bone is rotated 90 degrees from the body axes (most of them)
      must still stand flat."
