    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The guard-shape gate, stated as an executable fact rather than a comment.\n\n
      `NaN < 0.5f` is FALSE. So a validity check written as \"reject if bad\" waves
      NaN straight through --\n which is exactly how a guard that was written to
      stop a zero quaternion still let a NaN into the bones.\n The correct shape
      is \"reject unless good\": !(x > threshold), which IS true for NaN."
    Remarks: 
