  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: FootTargetRotation_SurvivesTheSolvesOwnOffsetMultiply
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (offset
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE CONTRACT. SolveTwoBone will multiply whatever we give it by the
      per-avatar offset. So the value we\n hand over, once that multiply has happened,
      must be the bone rotation we actually meant:\n\n     (footRot * offset^-1)
      * offset  ==  footRot\n\n Tolerance is 0.5 degrees: an inverse plus two quaternion
      multiplies in float32 leaves ~0.1 deg of\n round-trip noise. A real double-offset
      is tens of degrees (see the legacy gate below), so this is ~2\n orders of magnitude
      clear of the defect it guards -- loose enough not to be flaky, nowhere near
      loose\n enough to let the bug back through."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
