      the pre-cancellation away and hands the bone rotation straight over, the result\n
      is wrong by exactly the calibration offset. This asserts that the naive version
      really is badly wrong,\n so the round-trip gate cannot pass vacuously (e.g.
      if every sample offset were identity). A revert then\n fails loudly, with a
      reason, instead of silently reintroducing a bug that took a full day to find."
