  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisFootMocapQualityTests
    MemberName: BasisFootMocapQualityTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Does the procedural foot stepper WALK like a human?\" -- measured
      against real mocap.\n\n The stepper (BasisFootSimulateJob) synthesises feet
      from hips/head/chest; it never sees real feet. So\n this drives the REAL job
      from each walking clip's hips/head/chest and scores the SYNTHESISED feet\n
      against the clip's REAL feet, dimensionlessly (fractions of leg length / pendulum
      time) so the numbers\n transfer to any avatar size. It is the foot analog of
      BasisMocapMotionQualityTests (elbow/knee).\n\n Two things are gated, in order:\n 
      1. the MEASUREMENT LAYER -- the real-human numbers must match the biomechanics
      literature, or the\n     whole comparison is fiction (the recurring \"don't
      tune against a broken metric\" lesson);\n  2. the STEPPER -- its walk must
      fall inside the human envelope (double-support, clearance, slide, reach).\n\n
      See project_basis_foot_mocap_comparison_harness for the Python twin and the
      baseline this validates."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
