  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisFootRotationTests
    MemberName: BasisFootRotationTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Fast rotation around the hips must not make the feet step on each
      other.\"\n\n Drives the REAL BasisFootSimulateJob through a battery of in-place
      spins (both a PHYSICAL spin -- the\n playspace fixed while the body yaws, the
      hard case -- and a character-controller/stick turn) at chibi,\n adult and giant
      scale, and asserts the feet never overlap and never scissor badly. This is
      pure\n synthetic (no BVH), so it runs headless in the batch suite -- unlike
      BasisFootIKSweep, which is editor\n only and merely TOLERATED fast-rotation
      crossover. See project_basis_foot_mocap_comparison_harness.\n\n Also guards
      two bug CLASSES this system has shipped before: scale-dependence (a metre constant
      that a\n chibi feels differently) and framerate-dependence (a self-referential
      smoothing that converges by frame\n count, not time). The gait law is dimensionless,
      so both must be invariant."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
