    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: " <summary>\n Checks & balances on the stepper that need no mocap: a
      synthetic straight walk driven through the REAL\n job, asserting the invariants
      the gait law promises.\n\n  1. SCALE-INVARIANCE -- the whole reason every constant
      is a fraction of leg length: a chibi and a giant\n     must produce IDENTICAL
      dimensionless gait once size is divided out. The stepper was shipped broken
      on\n     small avatars once (a metre constant a chibi felt differently); this
      pins it.\n  2. FRAMERATE-INDEPENDENCE -- the stepper had blends that converged
      by frame count, not time (a foot in a\n     different pose mid-stride on a
      faster GPU). Same walk at 30/72/144 fps must match.\n  3. IDLE -- a standing
      person must not fidget: near-zero speed => near-zero steps.\n  4. FINITE --
      no NaN/Inf ever reaches the rig.\n See project_basis_foot_mocap_comparison_harness.\n
      </summary>"
    Remarks: 
