    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The desktop head carry (BasisHeadPitchSwingCore).\n\n A head pitches
      about the BASE OF THE NECK, not about itself, so the eye rides a lever arm
      and is carried\n FORWARD as the gaze tips down. VR gets this for free \u2014
      the HMD is a physical object on that same lever arm,\n which is exactly why
      the spine bend has to suppress the resulting hunch when a chest tracker is
      present\n (see BasisSpineLookDownHunchTests). Desktop pinned the eye over the
      hips and so had none of it: the gaze\n tipped, the cervical solve hunched the
      chest, and the head never went anywhere."
    Remarks: 
