  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: HumeralAxialArc_PerElevationBand_RefereesTheProposedEnvelope
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Load(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\u26A0 THE OCCUPIED ARC OF A CIRCULAR QUANTITY, NOT A LINEAR
      PERCENTILE RANGE.\n\n The axial angle lives on a circle, so p1..p99 of the
      raw numbers is WRONG the moment the\n distribution straddles +-180: a tight
      cluster sitting on the seam reports an arc of nearly 360\n deg. The first run
      of this file did exactly that and reported 355.6 deg for the [30,60) band --\n
      a number that would have looked like a spectacular finding and was an artefact
      of the seam.\n\n The correct statistic is the SMALLEST ARC CONTAINING A GIVEN
      FRACTION of the samples, which is\n seam-invariant by construction: slide a
      window of k = frac*n over the circularly-sorted angles\n and take the narrowest
      span. Rotating every sample by any constant leaves it unchanged."
    Remarks: 
