    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The OTHER half of \"does the avatar behave the same wherever you stand\":
      float32 precision.\n\n Equivariance above is a statement about the reference
      FRAME and is gated tightly. This gates\n DISTANCE, which is a genuinely different
      failure: a solve far from the world origin differences two\n large coordinates
      to recover a 30 cm bone, and the mantissa runs out. Nothing is wrong with the\n
      maths -- there is simply less of it left. Worth measuring rather than tolerating,
      because it is the\n number that says how large a world can get before the IK
      visibly degrades.\n\n Pure translation, so the solved pose must translate with
      it and every scalar must hold still.\n The measured curve is written to the
      test log."
    Remarks: 
