  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisKneeAnteriorReferenceTests
    MemberName: BasisKneeAnteriorReferenceTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The knee half-space guard's ANTERIOR reference must be BODY-frame,
      never limb-frame.\n\n THE DEFECT. BasisLegSolveInput.BendNormal did double
      duty: the no-hint fallback pole AND the\n anterior reference for the guard.
      With FBIKTrackerBendNormal (default ON) the rig driver derives it from\n the
      lower-leg tracker's live rotation, so \"anterior\" rode the user's SHIN. Tibial
      rotation alone then\n swept the guard's bite point across a stationary knee
      hint. Measured on the shipping solver, hint parked\n at a legal 70 deg and
      never moved: the guard engaged at 20 deg of tibial rotation and dragged the
      knee\n from 70.00 to 29.09 deg by 60 deg -- 41 deg of knee travel from an input
      that did not move.\n\n The user's report was \"the hint role for legs is slow
      to respond and goes across a snapping point\": once\n inside the guard's band
      the gain collapses (1.00 -> 0.47 at 90 deg, 0.04 by 105 deg, 0.00 by 150 deg)
      and\n at 180 deg the pole is antiparallel and the sign flips, a 178.6 deg step.\n\n
      The compression itself is CORRECT and deliberate -- KneeAnteriorHardDeg is
      strictly under 90 so the\n posterior half-space is unreachable, and a circle
      cannot be mapped continuously into an open arc while\n preserving which side
      the knee is on. So the fix is not to widen or smooth the guard: it is to stop
      the\n reference moving. The tracker-derived plane stays exactly right for the
      POLE."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
