  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisKneeDeepCrouchTests
    MemberName: BasisKneeDeepCrouchTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Deep-crouch knee direction, end to end through the real no-tracker
      path:\n BasisSwivelHintCore.BuildFrame/LegHint (swivel model + domain guard)
      -> BasisLegSolveCore.\n\n The bug these pin: descending to a full crouch with
      the feet under the hips walks the swivel model\n out of its fit domain (CMU
      has no frames with the foot under the hip at fractional reach), where its\n
      polynomial confidence dips and then RECOVERS to ~0.86 while the predicted swivel
      is garbage (-48 deg\n vs the true +90). The trust gate re-trusted it, the anterior
      half-space guard caught the posterior\n pole, and BOTH knees pinned dead-lateral
      at ~88 deg -- \"the legs go 180 out to the sides\" -- with\n 30-38 mm/frame
      clicks on the way in. The fix is LegDomainTrust: reach-based, multiplied into
      the\n model's confidence so under-hip folded legs ease onto the anatomical
      sagittal pole through the\n existing HintDistrust path."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
