  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisKneePopLocaliserTests
    MemberName: BasisKneePopLocaliserTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "WHERE DOES THE KNEE POP?\n\n The corpus table says the knee logs 36
      excess pops -- and it logs the SAME 36 whether it is handed no\n hint at all,
      the old lookup, or the fitted swivel model, while a real knee TRACKER drops
      it to 11. A\n number that does not move when its supposed cause moves is not
      being caused by that thing. So the pops\n are not the hint's, and guessing
      which line of BasisLegSolveCore owns them has a 0-for-5 track record on\n this
      project.\n\n This file does not guess. It reproduces the pop detector frame
      by frame and prints, for every pop:\n where it fired, how big it was in metres,
      what the REACH RATIO was there (the pole singularity lives at\n 1.0), which
      axis the solver used, and -- the control that matters -- whether the HUMAN'S
      OWN KNEE popped\n on that same frame.\n\n It is REPORT-ONLY on purpose. A localiser
      that fails the build is a localiser people delete."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
