  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisKneeSwivelHoldTests
    MemberName: BasisKneeSwivelHoldTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"The knee hint role can sometimes just start rotating back and forth
      slowly while all the trackers are\n still\" gate -- the SINGULARITY HOLD (BasisSwivelSmootherInput.HoldWhenSingular).\n\n
      Standing is pinned at the 176 deg max-extension cap, ON the pole singularity:
      the knee's lever arm off the\n hip->foot axis collapses (conditioning ~= 0.035),
      so the swivel angle is undetermined and any residual\n body-frame micro-motion
      -- postural sway pivoting the leg over a planted foot, which is NON-rigid so
      the\n body-relative measurement does not cancel it -- rolls the whole leg.
      The output is a slow (~0.3 Hz)\n oscillation.\n\n The tracked-knee path runs
      the One-Euro with ConditionOnPole OFF (the 2026-07-17 \"6x faster\" fix), so
      it\n is deliberately responsive -- and a responsive low-pass CANNOT remove
      a slow oscillation: a 1-1.5 Hz floor\n is nearly transparent to 0.3 Hz. Only
      a HOLD (zero passband at every frequency) can. The hold freezes the\n swivel
      where conditioning is below HoldCondHi and is the exact identity above it,
      so a genuinely bent,\n tracker-driven knee is untouched.\n\n Four gates:\n  
      1. A slow oscillation at a STRAIGHT leg is FROZEN by the hold.\n   2. ANTI-TAUTOLOGY:
      with the hold OFF that same oscillation LEAKS through -- proving the gate measures
      the\n      real defect and a revert fails loudly.\n   3. A BENT knee is byte-identical
      with the hold on or off (the 07-17 responsiveness is not re-lagged).\n   4.
      Releasing the hold from straight to bent EASES in -- it does not add a snap
      the legacy path lacked."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
