  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: AtFullExtensionTheKneeKeepsABoundedLeverArm
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - forward
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "At full extension the knee's response to the hint must be BOUNDED,
      not a snap. The old solver let the\n leg lock dead straight, so the pole degenerated
      (rho -> 0) and the knee HAD to stop following the hint\n entirely -- this test
      used to assert exactly that. BasisLegSolveCore.MaxKneeInteriorDeg now caps
      the\n leg a few degrees short of straight, so the knee keeps a small but non-zero
      lever arm and rides a\n small bend circle instead of a degenerate point. The
      anti-snap property is preserved (the circle\n shrinks CONTINUOUSLY to that
      cap radius -- see the two KneeDoesNotSnap tests), but now the guarantee\n is
      the stronger one: the knee is never on the axis, so it is never a free-spinning
      stick."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
