  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisLegIdleSwaySweepTests
    MemberName: BasisLegIdleSwaySweepTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Leg IK moves unnaturally while standing still\" sweep for the two-bone
      leg solver\n (BasisLegSolveCore, the stream-free port of BasisFullIKConstraintJob.SolveTwoBone).\n\n
      Scenario: stand idle with no leg trackers (3pt / foot-IK). The foot is planted
      (foot-IK target is a\n world-anchored plant, rotation = zero-quat sentinel
      = position-only) and the whole pre-IK leg\n translates rigidly with the body
      as it micro-sways. The solver pulls the foot back to the plant\n every frame.
      The complaint is that this small idle sway moves the knee/leg a visibly larger,\n
      unnatural amount.\n\n Mechanism this sweep isolates: near full extension a
      two-bone limb has very high gain. With equal\n segments L the knee's forward
      bulge is d = sqrt(L^2 - (chord/2)^2); its slope d(d)/d(chord) -> -inf\n as
      the chord (hip->foot distance) approaches 2L. So a tiny change in hip-to-plant
      DISTANCE -- which\n is exactly what a vertical HMD micro-bob or a fwd/back
      lean produces while the feet stay planted --\n swings the knee forward/back
      by a large multiple of the body's motion. A real standing leg keeps a\n soft
      bend and barely moves.\n\n The sweeps drive the solver the way BasisLocalRigDriver
      does for the no-tracker standing case:\n   Root/Mid/Tip = the rest-pose leg
      translated by the body offset (rigid pre-IK pose),\n   TargetPosition = the
      fixed plant, HintWeight = the foot-IK blend (~1), HintPosition forward of\n  
      the knee, BendNormal = the hip's right axis (KneeBendPrefLeft = hipsRot * right),
      so the knee\n   bends in the sagittal plane -- the same plane the body sways
      in.\n\n Knee/foot OUTPUT POSITIONS depend only on the input POSITIONS + the
      bend axis, never on the input\n bone rotations, so those are left identity
      here. \"Gain\" = world-space knee excursion / body\n excursion over the idle
      cycle; >1 means the knee moved more than the body (the unnatural pop).\n\n
      This is ISOLATED-SOLVER CHARACTERIZATION only -- every test passes and just
      prints the gain tables.\n The live IK pipeline conditions this sensitivity
      away (forward knee hint + foot/knee smoothing): the\n in-editor BasisIKSweepRunnerWindow
      leg gates pass, incl. \"stance flicker\" (0 oscillations at reach\n 0.99) and
      \"temporal+footnoise\" (knee jitter 7mm well-conditioned vs 68mm raw). So these
      numbers show\n where the raw two-bone solve is touchy near full extension,
      NOT a live bug -- the foot DRIVER, not\n this solver, owns standing-idle foot
      behaviour (see BasisFootIKSweep)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
