    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisLegMaxExtensionCapTests
    MemberName: BasisLegMaxExtensionCapTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE LEG MAY NEVER BECOME A FREE-SPINNING STICK -- the knee's twin of
      BasisArmFullExtensionTests.\n\n ================================================================================================\n
      At an interior angle of 180 degrees the knee's distance from the hip->ankle
      axis is EXACTLY ZERO:\n\n     rho = upper*lower*sin(interior) / d        =>  
      rho(180) = 0\n\n The knee lies ON the axis; its circle has collapsed to a point,
      and the SWIVEL that places it can no\n longer position it. Measured on the
      real BasisLegSolveCore with 0.2 mm foot nudges, |d(knee)/d(foot)|\n sits at
      ~2-3 across the whole envelope and then SPIKES to ~36x at reach 1.000 -- a
      1 mm foot-tracker\n jitter swings the knee 36 mm -- before dropping back to
      0.5x the instant the foot passes full reach.\n\n AND THE LEG LIVES THERE. BasisLegSolveCore's
      own swivel comment: \"standing lives there: footHeightOffset\n is clamped so
      the legs fully extend, which parks hip->ankle at ~= thigh + shin permanently.\"
      Standing is\n the most common pose in VR and it sits right on the singularity.\n\n
      \u2B50 The arm proved the fix is nearly free in reverse. BasisLegSolveCore.MaxKneeInteriorDeg
      = 175 gives up\n ~0.5 mm of leg reach and buys a ~1.9 cm guaranteed knee lever
      arm. 175 (a 5 deg standing bend) is the\n measured relaxed / single-limb-stance
      knee angle (Perry gait; young-adult quiet stance ~2-5 deg), so it\n reads as
      natural, not as a crouch, while moving the interior=180 singularity out of
      the reachable set.\n ================================================================================================"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
