  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisLegShinRollTests
    MemberName: BasisLegShinRollTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Gate for the tracker shin roll in BasisLegSolveCore.\n\n THE DEFECT.
      BEND/AIM/SWIVEL spend all three DOF on knee and ankle POSITION, so the shin's
      rotation about\n its own long axis is a by-product of the swivel that places
      the knee -- the leg has no tibial-rotation DOF.\n Cross a foot over the other
      leg (hip external rotation + ~30-40 deg of real tibial rotation on a flexed\n
      knee) and that rotation has nowhere to go but the ankle, whose axial ROM is
      ~5-10 deg. The result is the\n snapped-looking ankle the user reported. A lower-leg
      tracker is strapped to the shin and MEASURES the\n rotation; the solver was
      using only its position.\n\n WHY THE INPUT IS A BONE ROTATION, NOT THE RAW
      TRACKER. A calf strap's clock angle around the limb is\n arbitrary, and the
      lower-leg role gets no Recalibrated* rotation offset (those cover only head,
      hips,\n chest, feet, toes, shoulders). Comparing a raw tracker rotation against
      the shin would bake the strap\n angle in as a constant bogus roll. The rig
      driver maps it through BasisLimbRollStore's calibration\n reference first,
      so BasisLegSolveInput.HintRotation is the tracker-implied SHIN BONE\n rotation.
      StrapClockAngle_Cancels below is the proof that this is what makes the feature
      safe.\n\n A PURE ROLL MOVES NO JOINT: the knee pivots on the shin axis and
      the ankle lies on it, so the knee stays\n on the tracker pole and the foot
      stays on target. The position gates structurally cannot see this, which\n is
      exactly why it is allowed (same argument as BasisArmSolveCore's MidPostRoll)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
