  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisLegTwistSmoothingTests
    MemberName: BasisLegTwistSmoothingTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Legs twist when I stand very still and straight\" gate for the leg
      knee-swivel smoothing\n (BasisFullIKConstraintJob.SmoothKneeSwivel + BasisSwivelFilterCore),\n
      the leg analog of the arm's SmoothElbowSwivel.\n\n Mechanism: with no foot
      trackers the foot is a position-only plant (rotation preserved) and the leg\n
      runs near full extension. There the two-bone solver's bend axis is the knee
      BendNormal (= hips-right,\n raw and unsmoothed) and the knee pole follows the
      (hips-yaw-derived) hint, so any hips-yaw jitter\n while standing rolls the
      near-straight leg about the hip->foot axis -- a visible twist. The fix\n low-passes
      the OUTPUT knee swivel (One-Euro): high-freq jitter is killed at the cutoff
      floor while a\n real turn opens the cutoff and tracks with negligible lag.\n\n
      Two layers, both lock-step with the live code:\n   - the FILTER gate (synthetic
      swivel) proves BasisSwivelFilterCore rejects jitter yet tracks a turn,\n  
      - the SOLVER gate drives BasisLegSolveCore with a yawing bend frame at standing
      extension and shows\n     the same filter collapses the resulting raw knee-swivel
      excursion.\n\n The TRACKED-KNEE gate covers SmoothKneeSwivel's other entry
      point: a player with a physical knee/lower-\n leg tracker. The hint is then
      the tracked shin, which the leg solve reduces to a pole DIRECTION with a\n
      short lever arm, so a few mm of tracker jitter amplify into degrees of knee
      swivel (\"legs sway when\n moving\"). That leg runs the same output-swivel
      One-Euro but with the more-responsive Tracked* cutoffs\n (low floor kills the
      jitter; big beta keeps a deliberate shin swing from lagging).\n \"p2p\" = peak-to-peak
      knee swivel (deg) over the steady window; lower = stiller leg."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
