    Summary: "The headline measurement: how far is the avatar's elbow from a real
      human's, on real motion, using the\n elbow the product actually ships (the
      bend lookup)? Reported, not asserted, on first run -- there is no\n honest
      threshold until the number exists. Once it has settled, gate it here and it
      becomes a ratchet.\n\n The three synthetic-device rows ride along here so every
      row's number is printed in ONE table and can\n be read against its neighbours.
      Their VERDICT (BasisMocapAccuracy.Gate) is printed per row and the\n failures
      are listed under the table, but it is deliberately NOT asserted -- see the
      footer note below.\n The assertion that actually guards these rows is TheTrackerLadder_DegradesMonotonically."
