  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisPerSlotSmoothingTests
    MemberName: BasisPerSlotSmoothingTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Everyone's trackers move differently\" gate for the per-group smoothing
      tuning\n (BasisBatchPositionFilterJob / BasisBatchRotationFilterJob `tuning`
      array\n + BasisSmoothingProfiles).\n\n Before this, the batch filter took ONE
      set of one-euro parameters for all 15 slots, so a buzzing IMU\n hip tracker
      and a quiet lighthouse controller were filtered identically -- you could only
      tune the\n compromise. The parameters are now per-slot, fed from a per-group
      profile.\n\n These gates prove the mechanism rather than the tuning: that two
      slots in the SAME batch with\n different tuning genuinely diverge, that uniform
      tuning still behaves as one global setting did\n (so the shipped defaults are
      a no-op), and that Passthrough ignores tuning entirely.\n \"p2p\" = peak-to-peak
      output excursion over the steady window; lower = stiller bone."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
