  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: RescalingAtUnity_ReturnsTheOriginalPose_BitForBit
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (int
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE RULER GUARD, PART 1: at 1.0x the rescale must be a bit-exact
      identity on the POSE.\n\n Not by short-circuiting. BasisClipProportion deliberately
      has no `if (IsIdentity) return copy;`\n -- the full rebuild runs, and it comes
      out exact because it accumulates a DISPLACEMENT scaled by\n (scale - 1f), which
      is exactly 0f at unity, rather than reassembling positions from the parent\n
      (a + (b - a) != b in floating point). So this test can actually fail, which
      is the entire reason\n it is worth writing: an identity test that a `return
      copy;` makes true guards nothing.\n\n GUARDS: any FP drift, renormalisation,
      re-grounding or rotation touch introduced by the rebuild.\n If this fails,
      every mismatch number in this file is fiction.\n HEADROOM: zero by construction
      -- exact float equality on every component of every pose of every\n frame of
      all 20 clips (~13,785 frames x 22 joints x 7 floats). The one accepted looseness
      is\n that -0.0f + 0.0f = +0.0f, which `==` treats as equal and which cannot
      change any measurement."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
