  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: RescalingAtUnity_ReproducesEveryBaselineAccuracyNumber_Exactly
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - List<string>(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE RULER GUARD, PART 2: the 1.0x rescale must reproduce the
      EXISTING accuracy numbers exactly,\n through the real harness, on the mode
      that ships (ElbowField) and the mode whose numbers are\n quoted throughout
      this project (Lookup).\n\n Part 1 proves the poses are identical. This proves
      nothing downstream of them cares either --\n same seeding, same One-Euro state,
      same pops, same percentiles. Every numeric field of\n BasisMocapAccuracySummary
      is enumerated by hand on purpose: a helper that compared \"the summary\"\n
      would silently stop covering any field added later, which is the same class
      of quiet lie this\n file exists to prevent.\n\n Clip and Path are excluded
      and that is deliberate, not an oversight: BasisClipProportion always\n suffixes
      the name (no identity special-case, see above) and both runs are handed a null
      CSV path.\n HEADROOM: zero -- exact equality. BasisMocapAccuracy.Run is deterministic
      (no RNG, no time, and\n the ElbowField path does not touch the static swivel-dump
      accumulators)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
