  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: Rescaling_MovesOnlyTheTargetedSegments
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - List<string>(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE STRUCTURAL GUARD, AND IT IS THE ONE THE IDENTITY TEST PROVABLY
      CANNOT GIVE.\n\n At 1.0x every group scales by the same 1.0, so a parent table
      or group table that puts the wrong\n bone in the wrong group is INVISIBLE --
      the identity test passes with a completely scrambled\n mapping. This is exactly
      the failure shape this project has shipped before (a detector whose\n output
      was identical whether its cause was present or absent), so the mapping gets
      a guard that\n depends on the mapping.\n\n GUARDS: BasisClipProportion.k_Parent
      / k_Group. An arm-only rescale must scale the arm by exactly\n its factor,
      must leave the LEG untouched to the bit, and must not move the shoulder AT
      ALL -- if\n the shoulder moves, the arm sweep is silently also a torso sweep
      and its numbers mean nothing.\n HEADROOM: where a quantity is UNMOVED it is
      exact float equality (zero headroom, and correct: a\n bone whose group scales
      by 1.0f contributes exactly 0f to the displacement, so those joints come\n
      back bit-identical and any distance between them does too). Where a quantity
      is TRANSLATED or\n SCALED, 1e-4 relative is float noise on a difference of
      metre-magnitude coordinates -- the CMU\n root wanders several metres from the
      origin, so cancellation in (a + D) - (b + D) costs about\n eps * |position|
      / |bone| ~ 4e-6 in the worst case. It is not a tuned threshold: a bone in the\n
      wrong group moves the ratio by 0.20-0.30, four orders of magnitude clear of
      it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
