  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisShoulderDirectionTests
    MemberName: BasisShoulderDirectionTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Regression tests for the scapulohumeral shoulder pre-solve (BasisShoulderSolveCore),\n
      the stream-free math the live FBIK SolveShoulder and the offline BasisShoulderSweep
      both drive.\n\n The shoulder girdle (clavicle/scapula bone) follows a coupled
      fraction of the upper-arm SWING away\n from the bind direction, measured in
      the chest frame, with the humeral axial twist removed. The\n upper-arm direction
      comes from the elbow tracker when present (shoulder->elbow, flexion-independent),\n
      else from the hand target. These tests pin the properties that make it look
      human and keep it safe\n to ship default-on:\n\n   * BIND REST     -- at the
      bind arm direction the girdle does not move (the authored pose is kept).\n  
      * ELEVATION     -- raising the arm elevates the shoulder, monotonically, in
      the elevation sense.\n   * PROTRACTION   -- reaching forward / across the body
      protracts it; left mirrors right.\n   * TWIST-FREE    -- the girdle never rotates
      about the arm axis (a twist-following clavicle was\n                      tried
      and reverted; this guards the regression).\n   * ELBOW DRIVE   -- a bent arm
      (elbow up, hand low) elevates the shoulder from the ELBOW tracker;\n                     
      the hand-target fallback, seeing only the low hand, cannot -- the headline
      win.\n   * FRAME RIGID   -- the solve lives in the chest frame: rotating chest+arm
      rotates the result rigidly.\n   * BOUNDED       -- clamped, smooth under smooth
      motion, and stable under a noisy elbow tracker."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
