  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ShoulderSolve_IsContinuous_ThroughEveryGate
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - StringBuilder(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The girdle carries five separate gates -- setting (8-95 deg of swing),
      reach (a hard threshold at\n 0.7 softened by t^2), hang (0.75-0.92), rise (a
      deficit window), posterior (0.50-0.95) -- plus a\n depression crossover, an
      elbow-trust fade, and a magnitude clamp. Each is a place where the\n output's
      DERIVATIVE changes, and a derivative change becomes a VALUE change the moment
      anyone\n gets the algebra slightly wrong.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F AND THERE IS A 180
      DEGREE SWING IN HERE. `swing = FromToRotation(restDirL, armDirL)` is\n anti-parallel
      when the arm points to the OPPOSITE side of the body -- a right hand reaching
      to\n the left shoulder -- where FromToRotation abandons the plane and returns
      180 deg about an\n arbitrary axis, and QuatToRotationVector's `deg > 180` wrap
      sits on the same point. Both are the\n principal-angle seam this repo has already
      been bitten by twice, on a pose a user can reach."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
