    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "AT REST, THE AUTHORED CLAVICLE MUST COME BACK EXACTLY. Nobody has moved:
      the torso is at bind and\n the arm is at its bind direction, so the girdle
      has nothing to contribute and the bone belongs\n exactly where the artist put
      it. Given the UpperChest it does. Given the Chest -- whose bind\n differs from
      the UpperChest's by the rig's own spine tilt -- the clavicle is bent off the\n
      authored pose while the avatar stands perfectly still.\n\n This is also the
      case that makes the PAIRING load-bearing: reading the live rotation from one\n
      bone and the bind from another turns the girdle frame into a since-bind delta
      plus a constant\n offset, and the constant offset is visible with the body
      at rest."
