    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The girdle solve is FRAME-RELATIVE: rotate the parent and the arm together
      and the clavicle\n follows rigidly, contributing nothing of its own. This is
      why feeding the wrong parent shows up\n as error one-for-one with that parent's
      independent motion, and it is what makes the headline\n number above (30 deg
      of UpperChest motion, ~30 deg of clavicle error) a prediction rather than\n
      an observation."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
