    Summary: "The OVER-guarding case, and the reason the TrackerFinal clause is conditional.
      Callers that\n build the input with `= default` \u2014 BasisShoulderSweep,
      BasisShoulderCoupleSweep and\n BasisShoulderDirectionTests among them \u2014
      legitimately leave TrackerFinal zero while\n HasShoulderTracker is false, where
      it is never read. Guarding it unconditionally would decline\n the entire trackerless
      solve, i.e. silently switch the shoulder off for everyone.\n\n Mutation: drop
      the `i.HasShoulderTracker &&` from the guard. This test then fails."
