  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: HorizontalForwardReach_AddsNoRhythmRetraction
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - motion."
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "NO DOUBLE-COUNTING. Reaching forward the clavicle PROTRACTS, and the
      coupled swing's\n ProtractionFactor already owns that half of the horizontal
      plane. The rhythm must therefore add no\n retraction in the sagittal plane;
      all it supplies is the elevation-driven retraction the coupled\n swing structurally
      cannot.\n Scoped to the HORIZONTAL forward band, which is where the coupled
      swing's protraction is\n strongest and where the double-count would therefore
      actually happen. Above that band the\n retraction deliberately returns \u2014
      Ludewig reports clavicular retraction at full elevation in ALL\n planes, and
      up there the coupled swing's horizontal protraction has itself faded \u2014
      so this test\n pins the no-double-count region rather than banning the term
      from the sagittal plane outright.\n Mutation: drop the `(1f - forward)` factor.
      Retraction at the horizontal reaches the full\n elevation-driven value and
      this fails."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
