  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: PureHumeralRoll_MovesNoGirdle_OnTheControllerOnlyPath
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - horizontal
    - Vector3.up
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u26A0\uFE0F THE CONTROLLER-ONLY REGRESSION GUARD. Reported from headset:
      \"even in regular VR (controllers,\n no hint) I'm able to rotate my hand and
      break it.\"\n\n The rhythm is a function of HUMERAL elevation, and only an
      elbow tracker measures the humerus.\n shoulder->hand is humerus + forearm.
      A pure humeral axial ROLL with a bent elbow sweeps the hand\n around a cone
      while the humerus does not move at all, so an unguarded hand-driven rhythm
      invents\n elevation out of a gesture that has none. Measured on the unguarded
      term, arm out to the side at\n 90 deg of elbow flexion: 61.2 deg of phantom
      elevation and 7.51 deg of clavicle swing, against\n 0.00 deg before the term
      existed.\n\n Mutation: set rhythmTrust = 1f on the hand path. The 90 deg-flexion
      row swings 7.5 deg."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
