    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "THE FALLBACK BRANCH, and it is the one this repo has been bitten by
      before. The hand-path trust\n bound needs the baked segment lengths; without
      them there is no bound, and the choice of what to\n do then is load-bearing.
      `elbowTrust` originally failed CLOSED here and silently switched the\n girdle
      off for three offline callers. This one deliberately fails CLOSED in the opposite
      sense \u2014\n it falls back to the reach gate rather than to blanket trust
      \u2014 because on the hand path,\n believing an unmeasurable driver is exactly
      the reported controller-only defect.\n\n BasisFullBodyIK always bakes TposeElbowLength,
      so no live path reaches this branch.\n Mutation: make the fallback `rhythmTrust
      = 1f`. The folded-arm row then drives the full rhythm."
    Remarks: 
