    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards the axial-twist measure the shoulder slide uses to read the
      chest's yaw relative to the hips\n (BasisTwistSolveCore.SignedTwistAngleDeg).
      It replaced `chestLocal.eulerAngles.y`, which\n gimbal-locks the instant the
      chest pitches ~90 deg off the hips -- a deep forward bend on ANY rig, or a\n
      chest bone bound pitched near vertical -- and there flips ~180 deg, throwing
      a phantom counter-yaw into\n the shoulders.\n\n Two properties: (1) it is a
      bit-for-bit no-op in the normal regime -- a chest that only YAWS reads\n exactly
      like eulerAngles.y, so ordinary torso twist is unchanged; and (2) it stays
      CONTINUOUS while the\n chest pitches through 90 deg, where eulerAngles.y does
      not."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
