  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisSpineBindFrameTests
    MemberName: BasisSpineBindFrameTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"On some avatars the chest snaps left/right when looking down\" regression
      tests for the spine-bend\n distribution -- BasisSpineBendCore (the port of
      DistributeSpineBend).\n\n The pre-bend measures the forward/lateral bend as
      atan2 angles of the chest and head directions in\n the hips frame: pitch =
      atan2(dir.z, dir.y), roll = atan2(-dir.x, dir.y). \"The hips frame\" was the\n
      live hips BONE frame, whose rest orientation is a rig CONVENTION -- an FBX
      exported from Blender\n binds the hips rolled -90 deg about X, others bind
      it rolled about Z. On such a rig the frame's\n y-axis is not \"up the spine\",
      so a steep look-down puts the chest/head dirs near the atan2(z,y) pole\n and
      a head scan across center flips pitch/roll ~180 deg -- the chest snaps sideways.
      An identity-bind\n avatar never nears the pole, which is why it was \"only
      SOME avatars\".\n\n The facing TWIST in the same function already cancelled
      the bind (headRotLocal = HipsBind * invHips *\n headRot, \"cancels the live
      hips bone bind\" so its atan2 stays continuous across center). The fix is\n
      to measure the bend directions in that SAME bind-cancelled frame. That makes
      the pre-bend depend only\n on the pose relative to the hips' ANATOMICAL frame,
      not on the arbitrary bind convention -- and it is\n bit-identical when the
      bind is already identity (HipsBind * invHips == invHips there).\n\n These guard:
      (1) no snap when a ROLLED-bind avatar looks down and scans across center; and
      (2) the\n bend is INVARIANT to the hips bind convention for a fixed anatomical
      pose -- the property that, when\n it failed, produced the snap. Sign convention
      matches the rest of the spine suite: positive pitch\n command (AngleAxis(pitch,
      right)) is look-DOWN."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisSpineChestTargetTests
    MemberName: BasisSpineChestTargetTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
