    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE FIX, PINNED AT EXACTLY ZERO.\n\n The same pure-gaze sweep
      that makes the shipped core invent 10.4 degrees of chest pitch, run\n against
      the cue the rig now actually uses: the NECK, reconstructed rigidly off the
      head.\n\n The two lever arms cancel algebraically -- the head's orbit about
      the neck, and the neck's offset\n carried back along the rotated head -- so
      this is not damped or faded or clamped to something\n small. It is ZERO, for
      any gaze, at any angle, on any rig. There is nothing here left to tune,\n which
      is the entire point: a fade would just relocate the problem, as it did for
      the elbow."
