  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisSpineLookDownHunchTests
    MemberName: BasisSpineLookDownHunchTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Chest hunches forward when I look down\" regression tests for the
      spine-bend distribution\n (BasisSpineBendCore, driven by DistributeSpineBend).\n\n
      The forward pre-bend is inferred from the HEAD-TARGET position relative to
      the chest. In VR the\n head target is the HMD, which sits forward of the joint
      the head pivots on -- so tilting the gaze\n down swings the HMD forward and
      the bend misreads that pure look-down as a forward torso LEAN,\n hunching the
      spine/upper-chest forward (and the squish multiplier compounds it). With a
      chest\n tracker the real lean is already measured, so DistributeSpineBend drops
      the head-position-derived\n pitch/roll pre-bend (zeroes those weights) and
      keeps only the head-facing twist.\n\n These pin both halves: that a forward-swinging
      head DOES hunch the torso at the normal (no-tracker)\n weights -- so the suppression
      isn't a no-op someone can delete -- and that zeroing the lean weights\n (the
      chest-tracker path) removes the hunch while preserving the facing twist. Position
      drives the\n pre-bend, so the head is held level here to isolate it; the look-down
      is modelled as the HMD arcing\n forward, exactly what the live rig feeds in."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
