  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisSpineLookDownSweepTests
    MemberName: BasisSpineLookDownSweepTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Chest snaps out of the way when looking down\" regression tests for
      the spine-bend\n distribution -- BasisSpineBendCore (the port of DistributeSpineBend).\n\n
      The spine/upper-chest YAW follows the head's facing azimuth: twistY = atan2(headFwd.x,
      headFwd.z).\n That azimuth is undefined when the gaze is vertical (head looking
      straight down/up): the head-\n forward's horizontal projection collapses to
      zero and the angle flips ~180 deg across the pole.\n With the production yaw
      weights that flip clamps to the ~25 deg lateral limit, so the chest/upper-\n
      chest TWISTS SIDEWAYS the instant the gaze crosses vertical -- the \"snap out
      of the way\" a user\n sees when they look down (most visible with a chest+hips
      tracker, where the chest is otherwise\n pinned to the tracker so the spurious
      twist stands out).\n\n The fix fades the facing twist out as the gaze nears
      vertical (horizMag -> 0), so it can't snap.\n These guard that: the applied
      yaw stays CONTINUOUS through vertical gaze (the headline), is still\n PRESERVED
      through ordinary look-down (the fade must not kill normal twist), collapses
      toward ZERO\n past vertical (no sideways flick at the floor), and stays FINITE
      across the whole sweep.\n\n The pure-pitch cases hold the head straight above
      the hips to isolate the twist exactly like the\n offline BasisSpineBendSweep
      Pass B isolates it for yaw; the realistic case also slides the head\n down+forward
      as the gaze drops, so the bend pitch engages too. Sign convention matches the
      cervical\n suite and the live job: a positive pitch command (Quaternion.AngleAxis(pitch,
      right)) is look-DOWN."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
