  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisSpineTautBandTests
    MemberName: BasisSpineTautBandTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"The head/neck jitters when I stand looking almost straight ahead\"
      regression tests for the spine\n CCD -- BasisFullIKConstraintJob.SolveSequentialSpineIK.\n\n
      Standing upright, the virtual spine places the hips a full chain length below
      the head, which parks\n the CCD at the chain's full-extension singularity.
      A small head pitch then commands a mm-scale\n COMPRESSION through the HMD's
      neck-pivot lever (quadratic in pitch: ~1.4 mm at 8 deg) -- and a\n straight
      chain cannot shorten by aiming. Only a bow can, the required bow angle goes
      as\n sqrt(compression), and nothing constrains its plane. The loop burned all
      20 iterations failing to\n converge, and each frame's sub-mm tracker noise
      re-picked the bow plane: a sustained 0.25-0.38\n deg/frame neck/chest buzz,
      versus 0.003 outside the band with identical noise. Exactly straight\n (taut)
      was quiet and a real lean was quiet, which is why the report reads \"ALMOST
      center straight\".\n\n The fix is the taut band in SolveSequentialSpineIK:
      commanded compression is softened through a C1\n hinge (band = 1.5% of the
      chain's own reach), so noise-scale compressions leave the chain taut --\n where
      the shipped solve already stalled anyway, measured tip error unchanged to 0.1
      mm -- and real\n compressions pass through with an error that decays as band^2/compression.\n\n
      These guard: (1) noise inside the former buzz band no longer buzzes the neck;
      (2) the taut regime\n (target at/beyond reach -- the untouched code path) stays
      quiet and straight; and (3) a deep\n commanded compression is still actually
      solved, i.e. the band does not neuter real bends.\n\n ==============================================================================================\n
      CONFIGURATION (2026-07-22). This file used to build a rig that does not ship,
      in two ways:\n\n   MaxChestDeltaProperty was 30, production ships 90 (FBIKMaxChestDelta,\n  
      BasisSettingsDefaults.cs:1334 -> BasisLocalRigDriver.cs:1603). That field is
      not only the chest\n   TRACKER's clamp at BasisFullBodyIK.cs:414 -- SolveSequentialSpineIK:522
      reads it into `chestCone`\n   and every ReachHeadJoint sweep enforces it through
      ClampChestCone:583, so it shapes this CCD with\n   no tracker anywhere in sight.\n\n  
      spineAnatomicalRom was false, production ships true (FBIKSpineAnatomicalRom
      `_v3`,\n   BasisSettingsDefaults.cs:1427 -> BasisLocalRigDriver.cs:1637). GuardSpineJoint:676
      returns\n   immediately when it is false, so the anatomical envelope never
      ran here. The old comment said the\n   guard was \"left off so the test isolates
      the CCD itself\" -- a defensible thing to want, but it\n   meant the singularity
      was only ever characterised on an unguarded chain, and the guard runs LAST\n  
      inside ReachHeadJoint, i.e. it gets the final word on every joint the CCD moves.\n\n
      Both are now shipped values, and the envelope is BAKED (BuildSpineAnatomy below)
      -- setting the flag\n alone would have been decorative, because GuardSpineJoint
      also returns when ChainSpineRestFrames is\n not created and nothing in this
      suite built it.\n\n THE OLD CONFIGURATION IS STILL EXERCISED, as [TestCase]
      rows, so the singularity behaviour has a\n fixed point to be compared against
      rather than being silently redefined.\n\n WHAT MOVED. Only one measured quantity
      changes: DeepCompression_IsStillActuallySolved's residual\n tip error. Everything
      else (buzz, beyond-reach, continuity, scaling, aim, lordosis pin) is\n bit-identical
      across all four combinations, because the taut band converges those cases in
      zero\n sweeps and the guard has nothing to guard.\n\n PROVENANCE: measured
      by replaying these scenarios against the REAL BasisFullIKConstraintJob\n compiled
      standalone (Unity was unavailable -- the Editor held the project lock). Every
      assert in\n this file passes at all four cone/ROM combinations. The same harness
      reproduces this file's own\n previously recorded 20.4 mm / 33.5 deg deep-compression
      figure at relax 0.8, which is what\n identified the stale comment corrected
      below. NOT yet confirmed by an in-Editor run.\n =============================================================================================="
    Remarks: 
