      forward, and the\n left/right turn is an axial rotation about that ALREADY-FLEXED
      neck axis (which is what the\n cervical spine actually does). The flexed turn
      axis is what tips head-forward through the\n vertical pole -- turn a head about
      a perfectly upright axis and no extractor is in trouble."
