  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: Legacy_ElbowSwivel_BreaksUnderBodyTilt_WorldDownReference
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Vector3.zero
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Not every tilt exposes the elbow's world-down reference, which is why
      it survived review. With the\n arm out along body-X, a ROLL about world-Z changes
      the magnitude of the projected world-down but\n not its direction -- and refDir
      is normalized, so the roll cancels and the measurement looks fine.\n A PITCH
      about world-X rotates the arm about its own axis: the pole turns with the body
      while\n world-down stays put, and the full tilt leaks into the swivel. So this
      gate SEARCHES the tilt\n sphere for the worst case rather than trusting one
      hand-picked rotation."
    Remarks: 
