  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: TheModel_RefusesToExtrapolate_WhenTheControllerIsBeyondTheAvatarsReach
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - System.Random(31337
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 THE TEST THAT WAS MISSING -- AND ITS ABSENCE IS WHAT PUT THE
      ELBOWS UP BY THE EARS.\n\n The corpus only ever contains a hand ON the arm,
      so every test in this file used to drive the model\n with |tipLocal| <= 1.
      The LIVE RIG hands it the raw CONTROLLER TARGET, and a user whose arms are\n
      longer than their avatar's is outside that box on essentially every frame.
      A 3rd-order polynomial\n with coefficients up to 15 does not gracefully degrade
      out there -- it is a random number generator.\n\n So: put the target WAY past
      the avatar's reach, and the elbow must still be a sane elbow."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
