    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.BasisSyntheticTrackerTests
    MemberName: BasisSyntheticTrackerTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "GUARDS ON THE RULER.\n\n BasisSyntheticTracker is a MEASURING INSTRUMENT:
      every corpus number produced through it inherits its\n correctness. This project
      has already shipped several metrics that were quietly lying -- a pop detector\n
      that read the same count whether its cause was present or absent, and a smoothness
      metric that rewarded\n over-smoothed mush over a real human. Both passed their
      tests. An unguarded model becomes the next one.\n\n So the assertions here
      are on the MODEL, not on the solver:\n   * Ideal is a BIT-EXACT identity --
      which is what lets a realistic-tracker row be A/B'd against every\n     existing
      baseline without re-basing the baseline.\n   * Same seed, same answer, exactly.
      A test that changes its answer run to run is worse than no test.\n   * Each
      parameter moves the output in its expected direction AND ONLY IN THAT WAY.
      Stand-off must not\n     touch the jitter; slip must be low-frequency and not
      gaussian; jitter must be zero-mean.\n   * The magnitudes land in the documented
      physical ranges.\n   * The constants promoted out of BasisArmTrackerHintAuthorityTests
      are pinned, so a later edit cannot\n     silently retune numbers that were
      calibrated against a real user complaint.\n\n Several tests carry an explicit
      NON-VACUITY assertion (a live control, or a floor on how much signal was\n
      actually measured) because the characteristic failure of a test like this is
      passing while measuring\n nothing at all."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
