  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: StandOff_AndGlitches_DoNotDisturbTheJitterStream
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BentArm(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 STAND-OFF MUST NOT DISTURB THE NOISE, AND A GLITCH MUST NOT
      DISTURB THE JITTER.\n\n Every effect draws from its own stream precisely so
      that a parameter can be attributed in isolation.\n If they shared one stream,
      switching a glitch on would shift every subsequent jitter draw and an A/B\n
      between two configurations would be measuring the draw ordering, not the parameter.\n\n
      Two claims, both exact:\n   * the jitter RESIDUAL is unchanged (to float association)
      when the stand-off moves 0 -> 6 cm;\n   * the position on NON-GLITCHED frames
      is BIT-IDENTICAL between a run with glitches and one without."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
