  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: Slip_IsLowFrequency_NotGaussian
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BentArm(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 SLIP IS DRIFT, NOT NOISE, AND THIS SAYS SO WITH A LIVE CONTROL.\n\n
      A strap migrates over a session; it does not rattle. The discriminator is scale-free:
      the largest\n SINGLE-FRAME step as a fraction of the largest EXCURSION. A low-frequency
      drift covers its whole\n range in thousands of tiny steps; white gaussian noise
      of the same excursion covers it in one.\n\n The gaussian control is measured,
      not asserted from theory, so this test cannot pass by the gate\n having been
      set somewhere nothing could ever reach."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
