  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: ASlowDevice_HoldsItsLastSample_AndNeverInterpolates
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - oversampled
    - seconds
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\u2B50 A SLOW DEVICE HOLDS ITS LAST SAMPLE. IT DOES NOT INTERPOLATE.\n\n
      This distinction is the whole reason the update rate is modelled at all. An
      interpolated input is\n smoother than the runtime's, and a harness fed a smoother
      input than the runtime gets will report a\n solver that is calmer than the
      one that shipped -- which is exactly the class of blind spot the foot\n sweep
      already paid for once.\n\n The check is exact: every delivered position must
      be bit-identical to a truth pose the model was\n actually SHOWN. An interpolation
      would land between two of them and be a member of neither."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
