    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: AHipsTracker_SuppressesEveryPelvisSynthesisStage
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - LoadDispatchClips(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A HIPS TRACKER SUPPRESSES ALL THREE PELVIS-SYNTHESIS STAGES, EXACTLY.\n\n
      WHAT IT GUARDS: BasisFullBodyIK.cs:381 (ApplyTrunkCounterbalance), :395 (ApplyHipHinge)
      and :1033\n (ApplyCrouchBodyOffset). With `hasHipsTracker` true and LockHips,
      none of the three may run, so\n the solved hips bone must land on the commanded
      target BIT FOR BIT -- a tracked pelvis is the\n user's own measured pose and
      nothing is allowed to invent motion on top of it. That is the\n doctrine the
      removed hip-tilt-stabilization was removed for, and this pins it.\n\n The 3-point
      half is the other side of the same coin: with no hips tracker the pelvis MUST
      move,\n otherwise the synthesis stages are silently inert (they are fed by
      `standingHeadHeight`, which\n defaults to zero -- forgetting to pack it is
      exactly how this measurement would quietly become a\n no-op). Headroom: the
      untracked pelvis is required to move more than 1 mm on at least one frame;\n
      measured travel on a real crouch is centimetres."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.IK.
    MemberName: FootTrackers_DoNotPerturbTheSpineDispatch
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - LoadDispatchClips(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "FOOT TRACKERS DO NOT REACH THE SPINE DISPATCH.\n\n WHAT IT GUARDS:
      the honesty of the matrix table itself. \"4-point\" and \"6-point\" differ
      only by\n feet, and SolveSpine cannot see a foot tracker -- it branches on
      the chest and hips flags alone.\n So those two rows MUST be numerically identical,
      and if they ever diverge, either a foot flag has\n leaked into the spine dispatch
      or the harness has become nondeterministic; both make the whole\n table untrustworthy.
      Headroom: exact equality is required, not a tolerance -- the two runs are the\n
      same code on the same inputs."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
