    Summary: "World-space pose of this bone AFTER the full-body IK solve (the rendered
      bone), published by\n BasisLocalRigDriver once the rig evaluates. Unlike OutgoingWorldData\n
      (the pre-IK target the solver aims at), this is where the bone actually ended
      up. Published for every\n bone control after the rig evaluates; bones with
      no solved transform (center-eye, mouth, or a bone the\n avatar lacks) fall
      back to OutgoingWorldData. Zero/identity rotation until the first solve."
