  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.Desktop.
    MemberName: SetSuppressed
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Destroy(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Hard-suppresses the reticle while a feature needs the screen center
      clear\n (e.g. the handheld camera is out). Unlike SetEnabled/SetFocused\n this
      destroys the quad rather than deactivating it, and re-creates it on demand
      when\n suppression is lifted \u2014 provided the user setting and cursor focus
      still want it shown."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
