  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Calibration.
    MemberName: CapturedTrackerOffsets_ArePlayspaceInvariant
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 0.01f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The position offset a tracker captures at calibration must be play-space
      invariant: the\n reference bone is the avatar's T-pose bind anchored at the
      HEAD (ComputeTposeAnchor), and both\n the head and the tracker carry the same
      drag, so the captured inverse offset \u2014 tracker-local\n geometry \u2014
      must not change by a millimetre. This is what keeps a calibration taken while\n
      dragged interchangeable with one taken in place, and existing calibrations
      valid across drags.\n Exercises the REAL BasisCalibrationMath capture path
      end-to-end."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
