  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.UI.BasisUIToolkitPointerIdentityTests
    MemberName: BasisUIToolkitPointerIdentityTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Guards the one genuinely fragile part of the UI Toolkit integration.\n\n
      UI Toolkit models XR pointers but exposes no public way to construct one \u2014
      every public\n GetPooled overload derives its id from a mouse, touch or pen.
      BasisUIToolkitPointerIdentity\n binds the non-public setters once per event
      type. That binding is the thing a Unity upgrade\n can silently break, and the
      failure is quiet: pointers collapse onto one id and two hands\n start fighting
      over a single hover, with nothing logged.\n\n If Supported fails after an editor
      upgrade, the integration still works \u2014\n it has fallen back to a single
      pen pointer. Re-point the binding at the renamed member."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
