    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Registers every runtime language JSON as an Addressable with the\n
      `language` label that `BasisLocalization` loads at runtime.\n\n \n\nAny package
      can contribute strings, not just the framework: every\n `*.json` whose asset
      path passes through a `Localization/Languages`\n folder is discovered through
      the AssetDatabase, so it works\n regardless of how the package was added \u2014
      embedded under `Packages/`,\n referenced locally, or installed from a registry/git
      into the read-only\n package cache. Dropping `{code}.json` into\n `<your-package>/.../Localization/Languages/`
      is enough; files\n that share a language code merge by key at runtime, so a
      package only ships\n the keys it owns.\n\n\n\nThe SDK editor twin folder is
      excluded \u2014 those strings belong to\n `BasisEditorLocalization`, which
      loads from disk via AssetDatabase and\n must not ship in runtime bundles.\n\n\n\nRuns
      as both a menu item and an AssetPostprocessor so\n importing a package (or
      editing a language file) auto-registers it \u2014 no\n manual Addressables
      bookkeeping required. A content rebuild is still needed\n before the strings
      appear in a player build."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
