  - TypeFullName: Basis.MediaPipe.MediaPipeSpace
    MemberName: MediaPipeSpace
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "MediaPipe landmarks arrive in a y-down frame, and the backend mirrors
      the camera image before\n inference (selfie view), so the reported geometry
      is a mirror of the real body. Everything is\n converted into one Unity-space,
      un-mirrored, anatomically-labelled frame here so the converters\n never deal
      with raw MediaPipe conventions again.\n\n The hand landmarker already compensates
      for a mirrored image in its handedness LABEL (it assumes\n selfie input), but
      not in the landmark COORDINATES. The pose landmarker compensates for neither,
      so\n its left/right labels are repaired from geometry \u2014 see SideSwapNeeded.\n\n
      Depth needs no correction. MediaPipe's z grows AWAY from the camera, which
      is also the direction Unity's\n +Z runs once x and y are in true camera coordinates,
      so z passes through untouched. The user faces the\n camera, so their body frame's
      forward comes out as -Z, and a hand held toward the camera lands in front\n
      of the avatar. Nothing here depends on guessing that sign: x and y are unambiguous,
      and the frame's\n forward is derived from them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.MediaPipe.
    MemberName: IsFinite
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - v
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: " <summary>\n A landmark the maths is allowed to touch.\n\n The pose
      model can hand back a NaN, and NaN fails every ordered comparison \u2014 so
      a `< epsilon`\n degeneracy guard lets it straight through, the one-euro filters
      latch it and lerp it forward forever,\n and it finally reaches the Burst IK
      job where the arm-bend lookup does `(int)NaN` == int.MinValue and\n aborts
      the process. Every gateway below checks this before it computes anything.\n
      </summary>"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
