  - TypeFullName: Basis.MediaPipe.
    MemberName: SideSwapNeeded
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - PoseCount
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether the pose model's left/right labels came back reversed, decided
      from geometry rather than\n from what the model called them. The user is sitting
      in front of the camera facing it, so their\n LEFT shoulder is the one on the
      camera's right (larger x) \u2014 an x axis we trust, because only the\n depth
      axis is ambiguous. Returns +1 to swap, -1 to keep, 0 when the shoulders are
      too edge-on to\n tell (turn sideways and the caller should just hold the last
      decision).\n\n Trusting the model's labels instead is what put the arms behind
      the body: reversed sides flip the\n shoulder axis, which flips the body frame's
      forward, which lands a hand held at your chest behind\n the avatar's back."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
