  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.OpenVR.
    MemberName: ThreadedInputUpdate
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "When true the SteamVR action-state update (UpdateActionState + button/axis/skeleton\n
      reads \u2014 the bulk of the per-frame input cost) runs on a worker thread,
      kicked from\n SimulateKick and joined in Simulate so it overlaps the\n comms/network-apply
      work between the two. OpenVR interfaces are thread-safe, the\n update path
      reads main-thread state only via SteamVR_Input.CaptureMainThreadState,\n and
      no Basis code touches action state between kick and join (readers are the eye\n
      driver before the kick, and device polls after the join)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
