  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Constraints.BasisConstraintConversion
    MemberName: BasisConstraintConversion
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Rewrites Unity's built-in constraints and the Animation Rigging package's
      constraints onto the\n Basis equivalents, then removes the originals along
      with the rig that drove them.\n\n This is what lets constrained content run
      at all on a remote avatar. Animation Rigging needs an\n Animator and a PlayableGraph
      per rig, and remotes have neither \u2014 their bones come off the\n network.
      Unity's built-in constraints do run without an Animator, but each one costs
      its own\n component update and its own scattered transform reads, every frame,
      on every avatar in the\n instance. Everything converted here ends up in one
      batched Burst job instead.\n\n Conversion runs while the content is still parked
      inactive, so the originals never evaluate\n even once and there is no first-frame
      pop. Nothing here logs per component: a busy instance\n converts hundreds of
      these at a time, and the exception notifier fans errors out to disk and\n the
      network."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
