  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Constraints.BasisTwistChain
    MemberName: BasisTwistChain
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: BasisConstraintBase
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Spreads the twist between a chain's two ends across the bones in between,
      so a wrist or waist\n turn distributes along the chain instead of shearing
      at one joint. The Basis stand-in for\n Animation Rigging's `TwistChainConstraint`.\n\n
      Animation Rigging drives a whole chain from one component and samples an AnimationCurve
      at\n bind time to decide each bone's share. Basis drives one transform per
      constraint, so a\n converted chain becomes one of these per bone, each carrying
      the share the curve already gave\n it \u2014 which is also why no curve has
      to survive into the solve.\n\n Source 0 is the root end, source 1 is the tip
      end."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
