    Summary: "Analytic two-bone IK \u2014 the arm and leg solver. The Basis stand-in
      for Animation Rigging's\n `TwoBoneIKConstraint`.\n\n Sits on the tip bone (the
      hand or foot). The mid and root default to walking up the hierarchy,\n which
      is what a limb already looks like, but both can be set explicitly for rigs
      with spacer\n transforms in between. The IK target is the first source and
      the hint (pole) is the optional\n second, so both take part in the dependency
      ordering \u2014 an IK target that is itself constrained\n still solves first."
