    Summary: "LiteNetLib packet pool size. Must be large enough to avoid allocating
      new NetPacket\n objects during high-throughput send loops. With 1000 players
      at ~4M sends/sec,\n packets cycle through pool rapidly. 65536 keeps the pool
      warm and avoids GC pressure."
