  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: ServerInfoMinRequestBytes
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Minimum total request size (in bytes) the server will accept on an\n
      unconnected info query. Clients pad their query up to this size with\n zeros
      so the response is never larger than the request \u2014 that removes\n the
      bandwidth-amplification factor that makes UDP discovery protocols\n attractive
      as DDoS reflectors. Worst-case response is ~340 bytes\n (full-length name +
      MOTD), so 384 keeps the amp ratio < 1."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
