  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkUdpDropMonitor
    MemberName: BasisNetworkUdpDropMonitor
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Linux-only background sampler that polls /proc/net/snmp and warns when
      the kernel\n drops inbound UDP datagrams. Two failure modes show up here:\n  
      1) RcvbufErrors increasing  =>  receive thread can't drain the socket buffer
      fast\n      enough. Fix: raise MultiSocketCount (more recv threads sharing
      the port via\n      SO_REUSEPORT) or grow the kernel buffer (sysctl net.core.rmem_max).\n  
      2) InErrors > RcvbufErrors  =>  checksum/decode-level corruption, unrelated
      to\n      saturation. Indicates link/NIC issues.\n On non-Linux platforms Start()
      is a no-op."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
