  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkConsole.BasisSetupWizard
    MemberName: BasisSetupWizard
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "First-boot setup wizard. Runs once, before the network server starts,
      when no\n config.xml existed at launch (a brand-new server). It walks the operator
      through\n the core server settings and forces them to designate at least one
      admin, so a\n fresh server is never left misconfigured or with nobody able
      to moderate it.\n Admins are stored in permissions.xml as members of the \"admin\"
      group (full access),\n exactly like the runtime \"/perm user group add <uuid>
      admin\" command; the other\n settings are written straight back to config.xml."
