  - TypeFullName: Basis.MicrophoneCapture
    MemberName: MicrophoneCapture
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Captures a real system recording device (e.g. \"CABLE Output (VB-Audio
      Virtual Cable)\"),\n encodes it with the same Opus settings the simulated crowd
      uses, and publishes 20 ms frames\n for VoiceSender to transmit. Lets a load
      test carry actual audio a listener can judge,\n instead of a synthetic sweep.\n\n
      winmm/waveIn rather than WASAPI: no package dependency, and 48 kHz 16-bit mono
      is all the\n encoder wants. waveInGetDevCaps truncates names to 31 characters,
      so device selection is a\n case-insensitive substring match and every device
      is logged at startup."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
