  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkClientConsole.
    MemberName: GetSpawnPosition
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - GetRandomOffset(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A spawn point distributed uniformly over a horizontal disc of the given
      radius.\n\n This matters for load-test fidelity. The server picks avatar quality
      AND send interval per\n PAIR by distance (High under 10m, Medium 30m, Low 50m,
      VeryLow beyond), so clients spawned\n on top of each other put every pair in
      the closest, most expensive tier \u2014 a worst case no\n real instance hits.
      Spreading them over a realistic radius is what makes a \"resting network\n
      usage\" number mean anything.\n\n The sqrt keeps the distribution uniform by
      AREA; without it points bunch toward the centre\n and the effective spread
      is much smaller than the radius suggests. Y stays near standing\n height with
      slight variation, since players occupy a floor rather than a sphere."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
