  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarDeltaCompression
    MemberName: BasisAvatarDeltaCompression
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Server\u2192client avatar delta compression. A keyframe is the full
      fixed-size payload\n (BasisBoneRotationCompression.ConvertToSize). A delta
      encodes only the fields\n that changed since the last keyframe, each carrying
      its absolute value, preceded by a\n per-field dirty mask. Reconstructing a
      full payload = copy the baseline keyframe, then\n overwrite the dirty fields.
      Pure C#; shared by the server (encode) and client (decode).\n\n 56 fields:
      [0]=position(12B), [1..51]=51 bone rotations (bit-packed), [52]=scale(2B),\n
      [53]=body rotation(7B), [54]=hips delta(6B), [55]=hips rotation(7B).\n\n Delta
      body layout:\n   [dirtyMask:DirtyMaskBytes][changed byte-fields in field order][changed-bone
      sub-bitstream]\n The byte-aligned fields (position/scale/rots) are copied verbatim;
      the dirty bones are packed\n contiguously into a byte-aligned sub-bitstream
      via the existing WriteBits."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
