  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarIdleSuppression
    MemberName: BasisAvatarIdleSuppression
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Decides whether a freshly-encoded local avatar frame must be transmitted
      or can be\n suppressed as redundant.\n\n The avatar payload is fully quantized,
      so two byte-identical payloads reconstruct to the\n exact same pose on every
      receiver. Re-sending a byte-identical frame therefore changes\n nothing visible
      \u2014 it is pure wire redundancy. Suppressing it is lossless by construction;\n
      any real motion above the quantization step changes at least one byte and is
      always sent.\n\n A heartbeat still forces a periodic resend so a late joiner,
      or a receiver that lost the\n final pre-idle frame, converges to the correct
      rest pose and the receiver's interpolation\n window never starves for long.
      The receiver holds the last snapshot when starved, so the\n only observable
      effect of suppression is fewer packets, never a different pose.\n\n Pure and
      Unity-free so it is unit-tested in BasisServerTests alongside the codecs."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
