    Summary: "Per-user admin override for the Opus encoder bitrate (bits per second).\n
      The server keeps the override keyed by netId; when the targeted user's peer
      is\n connected, it pushes a UserOpusBitrateOverride message so the client applies\n
      OPUS_SET_BITRATE to its live encoder. A value of 0 means \"no override \u2014
      use the\n client's default bitrate\". State is cleared when the peer disconnects."
