  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.Utils.NtpPacket
    MemberName: NtpPacket
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: Represents RFC4330 SNTP packet used for communication to and from a
      network time server.
    Remarks: "Most applications should just use the NtpPacket.CorrectionOffset property.\n
      \n\n\n\n\n The same data structure represents both request and reply packets.\n
      Request and reply differ in which properties are set and to what values.\n
      \n\n\n\n\n The only real property is NtpPacket.Bytes.\n All other properties
      read from and write to the underlying byte array\n with the exception of NtpPacket.DestinationTimestamp,\n
      which is not part of the packet on network and it is instead set locally after
      receiving the packet.\n \n\n\n\n\n Copied from GuerrillaNtp project\n with
      permission from Robert Vazan (@robertvazan) under MIT license, see https://github.com/RevenantX/LiteNetLib/pull/236"
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
